{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/341562-preliminary-outline-for-changeling-the-lost-second-edition","id":341562,"title":"Preliminary Outline for Changeling: The Lost Second Edition","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Changeling: The Lost"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-12-15T22:03:30-08:00","id":341562,"title":"Preliminary Outline for Changeling: The Lost Second Edition","content":"<br /> <br /> Sorry. Been scarce. No fun in mental health land lately. But I'm getting back on the saddle. I'll try to get blogging and chattering soon.<br /> <br /> The outline's under review, and will be posted once it's been greenlit.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":70,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","user":"MachineIV","date":".  Asked to remove the link while under review. 12-16-2014, 06:51 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-15T22:18:23-08:00","id":341585,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> [Huntsmen] are bounty hunters, not dragons. </div> </div> </div>[Tv Tropes Smartass]Technically, a Huntsman could be a capital D Dragon, but that raises the question of (A) how they managed to get in a True Fae's good graces to the point where they became an effective second-in-command, and (B) why the solipsistic Fae thought that having a second-in-command in the first place was such a great plan. Good story hook, that.[/Tv Tropes Smartass]<br /> <br /> Seriously though, nice Outline. I love the implied icons system, kind of like anchors for living changelings. They <i>are </i>kind of like ghosts of long-destroyed people, eradicated in the crucible of the Durance. The difference is that a changeling is likely <i>more </i>than what they left behind..Also, love the fact that we have a create-a-Court system now, and the fact that mortal allies are called &quot;potential targets.&quot; And this is why Huntsmen were what the Chronicle was about, not the Gentry.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":180,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","user":"Leliel","date":". 12-16-2014, 01:22 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-15T23:52:04-08:00","id":341622,"title":"","content":"Looks cool. My only criticism is that we have to wait so long for the book. Can't you make your writers work faster?!? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-15T23:52:23-08:00","id":341623,"title":"","content":"I must have missed something - why are the Gentry not being included?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-16T00:11:52-08:00","id":341626,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/341562-preliminary-outline-for-changeling-the-lost-second-edition?p=341623#post341623\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I must have missed something - why are the Gentry not being included?</div> </div> </div> </div>I feel as though it would be too much of a statement of the obvious to point out how detrimental putting the Others front and center was to their credibility as distant fae antagonists who largely work through catspaws instead of alternately roving TPKs and laughable excuses for godlike beings. Also, wordcount being at a premium, it's important to focus the antagonists section on antagonists that actually need stats.<br /> <br /> I mean, having just finished rereading Autumn Nightmares last week I can appreciate that &quot;True Fae&quot; is technically a wide spectrum of power, but they're explicitly harmed by prolonged stays on Earth without the excuse of &quot;here by obligation&quot; and the systems necessary to mitigate that are more than can ostensibly be spared for a line with as many existing subsystems as Changeling already has. The Fae got entire chapters to themselves in <i>two</i> 1e books; if they're going to be done justice in 2e it's not going to be by squeezing them in as a blurb the same size as hobs get.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":111,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","user":"Satchel","date":". 12-16-2014, 03:14 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-16T01:04:55-08:00","id":341643,"title":"","content":"If it's &quot;we have plans to cover them better further on&quot; I'm relatively ok with that - but leaving something so central out at this point worries me. The Fae as both stories and characters WITH WHOME YOU HAVE A PERSONAL RELATIONSHIP, is part of the unique feel of CtL to me. If the paranoia becomes faceless, I don't see the distinction from what DtD does with the God Machine.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-16T03:06:55-08:00","id":341701,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/341562-preliminary-outline-for-changeling-the-lost-second-edition?p=341643#post341643\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If it's &quot;we have plans to cover them better further on&quot; I'm relatively ok with that - but leaving something so central out at this point worries me. The Fae as both stories and characters WITH WHOME YOU HAVE A PERSONAL RELATIONSHIP, is part of the unique feel of CtL to me. If the paranoia becomes faceless, I don't see the distinction from what DtD does with the God Machine.</div> </div> </div> </div>It has a face; it just doesn't have stats. They're not antagonists, they're plot hooks. So they'll get attention in the Storytelling chapter, not the Antagonists chapter.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-16T03:34:25-08:00","id":341729,"title":"","content":"Looks super neat. I like that the antagonists (save Loyalists, for obvious reasons) use the simplified spirit rules, it makes so much easier to create some of your own.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-16T04:16:57-08:00","id":341734,"title":"","content":"I like that a lot of the antagonists are switching to the simplified spirit stat rules, will help keep things level. Always found it weird that an incubus (as an example) had full Fae stats in changeling books but similar creature in Mage or the like used the ephemeral rules.<br /> <br /> Speaking of which, will the Changeling book have the ephemeral rules with an add on for hedge stuff (and is certain fae/hedge stuff ephemeral now or just using simplified traits?), or will it only have a 'fae' system that happens to use power/finesse/resistance, sort of like Strix in vamp?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/themes/stvault/images/affiliatebanner4.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Christopher%20Falco&amp;affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\">Storytellers' Vault supplements (WoD, CoD)</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/FalconianP\" target=\"_blank\">My Patreon! (CofD bonuses include: Fae Sorcery/Technomancy for Vampires, Quick Conversion for Inferno, and more!)</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1130-falco1029","name":"falco1029","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1130_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1045"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-16T04:30:51-08:00","id":341743,"title":"","content":"I love the concept behind the Huntsman. For some reason, I originally thought they were just True Fae, but I'm delighted to find I was wrong. It's good to have Changeling antagonists other than, well, the Others.<br /> <br /> I do hope that the True Fae aren't changed -too- much when they are finally covered, I'd like to be able to use some the stuff from Equinox Roads and whatnot. I'm pretty glad they are becoming more distant, but no less personal: Makes it all the more terrifying when they do finally show up.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Raksi plays Peek-a-boo for keeps. ~ nalak42","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/203-kleptomania","name":"Kleptomania","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar203_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"557"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-16T04:54:38-08:00","id":341778,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I feel as though it would be too much of a statement of the obvious to point out how detrimental putting the Others front and center was to their credibility as distant fae antagonists who largely work through catspaws instead of alternately roving TPKs and laughable excuses for godlike beings. Also, wordcount being at a premium, it's important to focus the antagonists section on antagonists that actually need stats.<br /> <br /> I mean, having just finished rereading Autumn Nightmares last week I can appreciate that &quot;True Fae&quot; is technically a wide spectrum of power, but they're explicitly harmed by prolonged stays on Earth without the excuse of &quot;here by obligation&quot; and the systems necessary to mitigate that are more than can ostensibly be spared for a line with as many existing subsystems as Changeling already has. The Fae got entire chapters to themselves in two 1e books; if they're going to be done justice in 2e it's not going to be by squeezing them in as a blurb the same size as hobs get. </div> </div> </div>The True Fae I currently construct is more proactive in pursuing enemies or entertainment, but I also established he is an oddity and abberation in that matter, so generally True Fae in my intepretation are distant antagonists or do not care.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cI am absolute, I am perfect, I am supreme. I shall be eternal. My tragedy, is that there is no other fate for me. My powerlessness was that I couldn\u2019t subjugate my journey to the gods, while dreaming of rebirth at the end of distant time, like other pharaohs.\u201d Ramesses II, Fate/Prototype: Argent Fragments.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2918-kat","name":"Kat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2918_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1762"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-16T07:42:00-08:00","id":341877,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/341562-preliminary-outline-for-changeling-the-lost-second-edition?p=341626#post341626\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I feel as though it would be too much of a statement of the obvious to point out how detrimental putting the Others front and center was to their credibility as distant fae antagonists who largely work through catspaws instead of alternately roving TPKs and laughable excuses for godlike beings. Also, wordcount being at a premium, it's important to focus the antagonists section on antagonists that actually need stats.<br /> <br /> I mean, having just finished rereading Autumn Nightmares last week I can appreciate that &quot;True Fae&quot; is technically a wide spectrum of power, but they're explicitly harmed by prolonged stays on Earth without the excuse of &quot;here by obligation&quot; and the systems necessary to mitigate that are more than can ostensibly be spared for a line with as many existing subsystems as Changeling already has. The Fae got entire chapters to themselves in <i>two</i> 1e books; if they're going to be done justice in 2e it's not going to be by squeezing them in as a blurb the same size as hobs get.</div> </div> </div> </div>That, and hiring/creating Huntsmen is perfectly in character for True Fae. It shoves the work on someone who doesn't find Earth as hazardous to their health, and, to be frank, Huntsmen are specialized for the job. A few of them are simply better at it than their masters.<br /> <br /> I would like to know what happens to contagion-dreams, though, and Incubi. Both are elements of oneriomancy I love. Maybe dream poison is part of the Huntsman's arsenal?<br /> <br /> Also, I already have a crossover idea; the mercenary shapeshifters and the ultimate hunters. Two enter, one leaves.<br /> <br /> Huntsman vs Uratha.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-16T08:42:27-08:00","id":341937,"title":"","content":"I might have missed something but I saw no mention of where is the Hedge. I assume it is in the Storyteller's Chapter? And what about Tokens?<br /> Really liked the outline, and the idea of the Huntsmen.Be very afraid of toasters guys!<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4055-felipe","name":"Felipe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4055_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"538"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-16T09:45:32-08:00","id":342025,"title":"","content":"Oh, and what about Entitlements?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4055-felipe","name":"Felipe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4055_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"538"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-16T09:59:30-08:00","id":342057,"title":"","content":"My Changeling The Lost urges are finally sated, at least in part, by this thread. Anticipating this even more now.<br /> <br /> The Huntsmen actually sound very interesting, even if before this I saw the archtype they seem to embody as another form or whim of the True Fae. Such as the Arcadian Huntsman in the first edition core book. I dig their concept a lot, but I am concerned by how scary their flexibility of form that's mentioned actually is. It almost makes them scarier than True Fae to consider as enemies, and I feel like that might shift the constant but ephemeral paranoia of first edition to very real and claustrophobic nightmares in a Changeling's life. I'm also wondering exactly what kind of entities they are. Are they still faerie beings, but different in essence from hobgoblins, faerie beasts and True Fae, and if yes, then how so?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","name":"YeOfLittleFaith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar188_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-16T09:59:47-08:00","id":342058,"title":"","content":"I don't imagine that Entitlements need to be changed all that much from 1E, if at all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/747-knowbody","name":"Knowbody","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"391"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-16T10:23:48-08:00","id":342070,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>YeOfLittleFaith</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/341562-preliminary-outline-for-changeling-the-lost-second-edition?p=342057#post342057\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I dig their concept a lot, but I am concerned by how scary their flexibility of form that's mentioned actually is. It almost makes them scarier than True Fae to consider as enemies, and I feel like that might shift the constant but ephemeral paranoia of first edition to very real and claustrophobic nightmares in a Changeling's life.</div> </div> </div> </div>As an addendum to this: I'm basically somewhat concerned the Huntsmen might overshadow the True Fae as an ephemeral background presence that incites not always justified paranoia and madness. Because instead they'll be enforcing very real and claustrophobic concerns that Changelings have to always live with. They can still play into the difficulty Changelings are supposed to have with distinguishing reality from dreams and not letting their nightmares suffocate their view of the world, but...<br /> <br /> To me, it could very easily miss the mark of what the antagonists of Changeling The Lost and some of its themes are about, depending on how their concept is explored. They make me think more of Demon than Changeling, or how a friend of mine I just discussed this with put it, &quot;they're the Angels of Changeling The Lost&quot;. Now, I might be biased, because while I love Demon The Descent, I am unable to get into character as one without the unease and anxiety doing bad things to me. That, and I love the shit out of the True Fae as antagonists in the World Of Darkness period.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","name":"YeOfLittleFaith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar188_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-16T10:41:38-08:00","id":342082,"title":"","content":"Very glad to see this! Thanks for posting the preliminary outline. ^_^ I've never read one before, and I always like a peek backstage.<br /> <br /> I'm making my way through slowly in bits and pieces. I'm only past Chapter 2, now. I think I expected something slightly different for Seeming/Kith, but I like what I see. In particular, I'mpleasantly staggered at the thought of around 100 Kiths in there. Impressive, ambitious, and avoids fans of Winter Masques Kiths feeling like they need to wait even longer to see them again.<br /> <br /> Observations and musings from the peanut gallery<br /> - I admit part of me wonders (as I'm sure you considered, in your deliberation) whether there'd be value in aiming for fewer Kiths with more wordcount apiece, going into more detail and covering more in additional supplements. Even with only 3/6 Seeming examples, that feels like an impressive amount to squeeze into just 250 words. Though of course there's value in both approaches, and this one likely jives better with your priorities and goals as a developer. Devil's advocate is simply a game I find fun, and I'm always interested in designer commentary, if they're interested in sharing it.<br /> - I have some mild disappointment that neither Seeming nor Kith has a Curse attached. I found them to be flavorful and interesting potential components for a unique playstyle (at least in principle). That said, there are lots of ways to get to such a playstyle, Seeming Contracts (unless much changed from that thread a ways back) kinda work with the idea, and -- especially with wordcount as tight as it is for each Kith -- the Curses still feel like a pretty uncontroversial thing to drop. Though I'd certainly be pleased by any further thoughts you had around your decision.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-16T12:45:13-08:00","id":342147,"title":"","content":"Oooh this is exciting.<br /> <br /> I have many questions, but I figure most of them will be best resolved by waiting until the finished book comes out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1423-espritdecalmar","name":"espritdecalmar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1423_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-16T15:50:46-08:00","id":342352,"title":"","content":"Just an FYI, I'm pulling the link at request while it gets reviewed. I'll try to address the stuff that was brought up, particularly in Gaius's comments there. It's mostly just stuff that slipped my mind. But, that's why I posted it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-16T15:55:27-08:00","id":342357,"title":"","content":"Probably toning down presence of Huntsmen would be a sensible approach. Occassional, but real threat, not bogeymen that are main concern. Simply, there should be a sort of balance.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cI am absolute, I am perfect, I am supreme. I shall be eternal. My tragedy, is that there is no other fate for me. My powerlessness was that I couldn\u2019t subjugate my journey to the gods, while dreaming of rebirth at the end of distant time, like other pharaohs.\u201d Ramesses II, Fate/Prototype: Argent Fragments.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2918-kat","name":"Kat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2918_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1762"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-16T20:09:49-08:00","id":342543,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kat</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/341562-preliminary-outline-for-changeling-the-lost-second-edition?p=342357#post342357\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Probably toning down presence of Huntsmen would be a sensible approach. Occassional, but real threat, not bogeymen that are main concern. Simply, there should be a sort of balance.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm guessing they're much closer to the Strix than the Idigam in terms of comparable plot-drivers from the other 2e chronicle-book-namers. (Definitely closer to either of those than to the Fallen World.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-17T00:07:50-08:00","id":342698,"title":"","content":"I appreciated the post-up nonetheless; drew a few conclusions, but I mainly felt that I didn't see a thematic tightening. I'll wait for some blog posts or write-ups before I give any weight to those conclusions, but yeah, little bit worried in the same vein as YeOfLittleFaith. Also didn't understand Icons at all, from a design perspective. Not really an outline's job to do, so... will wait, will see.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I call the Integrity-analogue the &quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/822559-trying-to-understand-the-morality-system?p=825008#post825008\" target=\"_blank\">subjective stat</a>&quot;.<br /> An explanation how to <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/913221-using-social-manuevering\" target=\"_blank\">use Social Manuevering</a>.<br /> Guanxi Explanations: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=787824#post787824\" target=\"_blank\">1</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=788173#post788173\" target=\"_blank\">2</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/833863-mages-and-trading-favors?p=834531#post834531\" target=\"_blank\">3</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2758-errol216","name":"Errol216","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-17T00:18:48-08:00","id":342703,"title":"","content":"-misses the outline-<br /> -wails in pain and confusion-","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/209-that-other-guy","name":"That Other Guy","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"702"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-17T00:18:54-08:00","id":342704,"title":"","content":"Sorry if I repeat myself but, do changelings have a free-form sorcery,goblin vow style this time, or they stick to the old level 1-5 fixed powers?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2411-raistlin","name":"Raistlin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"713"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-17T01:11:10-08:00","id":342712,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>YeOfLittleFaith</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/341562-preliminary-outline-for-changeling-the-lost-second-edition?p=342057#post342057\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Huntsmen actually sound very interesting, even if before this I saw the archtype they seem to embody as another form or whim of the True Fae. Such as the Arcadian Huntsman in the first edition core book. I dig their concept a lot, but I am concerned by how scary their flexibility of form that's mentioned actually is. It almost makes them scarier than True Fae to consider as enemies, and I feel like that might shift the constant but ephemeral paranoia of first edition to very real and claustrophobic nightmares in a Changeling's life. I'm also wondering exactly what kind of entities they are. Are they still faerie beings, but different in essence from hobgoblins, faerie beasts and True Fae, and if yes, then how so?</div> </div> </div> </div>I have a bit the same problem. I will run a game about <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/314862-krampus-in-ctl\">Krampus</a> stealing &quot;naughty&quot; people on Christmas Eve - would he still be True Fae, or just Huntsman now? What about Arcadian Huntsman from <b>CtL</b> 1ed itself?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-17T02:42:09-08:00","id":342745,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>That Other Guy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/341562-preliminary-outline-for-changeling-the-lost-second-edition?p=342703#post342703\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">-misses the outline-<br /> -wails in pain and confusion-</div> </div> </div> </div>I feel your pain brother. Hopefully it will be back up soon.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-17T04:19:43-08:00","id":342783,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I will run a game about Krampus stealing &quot;naughty&quot; people on Christmas Eve - would he still be True Fae, or just Huntsman now? </div> </div> </div>Whatever floats your boat, Changeling The Lost is so varied that it frankly sometimes provide too much options.<br /> <br /> Also, Yolfu brought up possibility in our talk that maybe Huntsmen given their bounty hunter theme could be hired by other parties than True Fae, even Changelings. The only questions is the proper price for their services.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cI am absolute, I am perfect, I am supreme. I shall be eternal. My tragedy, is that there is no other fate for me. My powerlessness was that I couldn\u2019t subjugate my journey to the gods, while dreaming of rebirth at the end of distant time, like other pharaohs.\u201d Ramesses II, Fate/Prototype: Argent Fragments.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2918-kat","name":"Kat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2918_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1762"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-17T04:45:46-08:00","id":342818,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/341562-preliminary-outline-for-changeling-the-lost-second-edition?p=342712#post342712\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I have a bit the same problem. I will run a game about <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/314862-krampus-in-ctl\">Krampus</a> stealing &quot;naughty&quot; people on Christmas Eve - would he still be True Fae, or just Huntsman now? What about Arcadian Huntsman from <b>CtL</b> 1ed itself?</div> </div> </div> </div>My problem isn't the confusion between them. It's that I fear the Huntsmen eclipsing the True Fae as the defining antagonists (behind the scenes and not) of Changeling The Lost. Say what you will, but to me, the Gentry have always felt like the one grand enemy of the Lost behind the curtains. Sometimes they're not there at all, sometimes they're pulling strings behind it, and rarely they pull it open and present themselves as actors in the play.<br /> <br /> Changeling The Lost is primarily about the Lost themselves, of course. But as their main opposition, the Fae are very important. (In fact, we've been told in this very thread they're in the Storytelling chapter and not the antagonists one.)<br /> <br /> Not to go back to Demon again, as they have very different themes and motifs, but the analogy is fitting: Demon is about the Unchained, their struggle for Hell, their rebellion, and their conflict for identity. The most visible enemies are Angels and cultists. But the true, defining antagonist, whose shadow is felt on every oddity they encounter, isn't any of them - it's the God-Machine, who drives it all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":188,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","user":"YeOfLittleFaith","date":". 12-17-2014, 08:00 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","name":"YeOfLittleFaith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar188_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-17T06:54:09-08:00","id":342890,"title":"","content":"About the Huntsmen thing(while I didn't get to see the outline and therefore know nothing), maybe make them avatars or slivers of Them, made as a way for them to experience and do things on Ironside?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-17T07:20:07-08:00","id":342899,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> About the Huntsmen thing(while I didn't get to see the outline and therefore know nothing), maybe make them avatars or slivers of Them, made as a way for them to experience and do things on Ironside? </div> </div> </div>&gt;Actors<br /> <br /> Been there, done that.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cI am absolute, I am perfect, I am supreme. I shall be eternal. My tragedy, is that there is no other fate for me. My powerlessness was that I couldn\u2019t subjugate my journey to the gods, while dreaming of rebirth at the end of distant time, like other pharaohs.\u201d Ramesses II, Fate/Prototype: Argent Fragments.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2918-kat","name":"Kat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2918_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1762"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-17T08:36:36-08:00","id":342959,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kat</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/341562-preliminary-outline-for-changeling-the-lost-second-edition?p=342899#post342899\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> &gt;Actors<br /> <br /> Been there, done that.</div> </div> </div> </div> Curse my lack of all the books!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-17T09:05:18-08:00","id":343010,"title":"","content":"Actually, a question. Do Loyalists not have Seemings? Because you would think since, in a certain way, they never actually escaped their Durance or took back their Kith from their Keeper, they lack the power that comes from that agency. I suppose it's debatable, since some of them may believe they did in fact escape, or may serve the Gentry without being aware of it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","name":"YeOfLittleFaith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar188_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-17T12:04:18-08:00","id":343129,"title":"","content":"about the 100 kirths, i think that having less of them and examples of the 6 seemings instead of 3 would be better. If for example under the draconic kirt i only have fairest beast and elemental im going to subconsciously start thinking that wizened ogres and darkling dont have it","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1351-sakii","name":"Sakii","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1351_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-17T12:44:49-08:00","id":343146,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>YeOfLittleFaith</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/341562-preliminary-outline-for-changeling-the-lost-second-edition?p=343010#post343010\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Actually, a question. Do Loyalists not have Seemings? Because you would think since, in a certain way, they never actually escaped their Durance or took back their Kith from their Keeper, they lack the power that comes from that agency. I suppose it's debatable, since some of them may believe they did in fact escape, or may serve the Gentry without being aware of it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Given how Loyalists are generally presented as going back to the Gentry after their escape, I'd say they have Seemings; the idea is that they gained their autonomy, but went back (or were blackmailed back) into the services of the True Fae. So they gained it, but lost it.<br /> <br /> Some, like Myra the Sphinx (Night Horrors: Grim Fears) I'm a little less certain about, but with her the idea is that she's become addicted to an abusive relationship with her Keeper. If she was okay with being kicked out, she wouldn't be in the pact that makes her a serial abductor now.<br /> <br /> Does make me wonder if non-Loyalist Wild Sam has a Seeming, though, seeing as how his Keeper just got bored of him as a friend, but decided to be nice and let him live his own life.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-17T12:50:35-08:00","id":343148,"title":"","content":"I admit I forgot about those cases. Well, logically speaking it seems like it might depend on the circumstances.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","name":"YeOfLittleFaith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar188_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-17T20:10:04-08:00","id":343601,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leliel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/341562-preliminary-outline-for-changeling-the-lost-second-edition?p=343146#post343146\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Given how Loyalists are generally presented as going back to the Gentry after their escape, I'd say they have Seemings; the idea is that they gained their autonomy, but went back (or were blackmailed back) into the services of the True Fae. So they gained it, but lost it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Or, to pull a lovely thing I overlooked from my first read through the corebook, don't <i>know</i> they lost it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-18T13:45:21-08:00","id":344082,"title":"","content":"But about those changelings that were made from mortals that just get lost in Hedge, and maybe survived in Arcadia on themselves? Are they now Seeming-less, as they did not free themselves? They got Kiths, even if they weren't remade in to those roles by the Keepers? With so central Kiths now, how could one be Kithless?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-18T14:19:40-08:00","id":344106,"title":"","content":"Why you say they didn't free themselves? If they managed to find their way back from Arcadia that counts in my book. Also, Arcadia seems to change people by itself, no need of an evident Keeper guiding the change to get a Kith.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-18T20:09:51-08:00","id":344335,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/341562-preliminary-outline-for-changeling-the-lost-second-edition?p=344082#post344082\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But about those changelings that were made from mortals that just get lost in Hedge, and maybe survived in Arcadia on themselves?</div> </div> </div> </div>You're going to have to clarify what you mean by &quot;survived in Arcadia by themselves,&quot; seeing as at least one reading of that phrase is a metaphysical impossibility.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-18T20:46:58-08:00","id":344341,"title":"","content":"I've been ignoring Wyrd on this one explicitly because one can't survive in Arcadia without accepting a pledge with the True Fae. Once Hospitality applies, you're beginning down the rabbit hole.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-18T23:08:51-08:00","id":344403,"title":"","content":"I missed the outline, so perhaps someone can tell me if pulling a Snow White is an option? I mean, giving the fairy tale themes that crop up in Changeling, the first thing I imagined when I heard the Huntsmen was the guy from Snow White who tells the Queen he's killed the Princess, but really didn't. I presume there's a section on escaping the huntsmen, but I'm curious if enticing/suborning/tricking/or otherwise manipulating the Huntsmen is possible (since I don't actually even know what they are).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-18T23:29:14-08:00","id":344429,"title":"","content":"As I only reread corebook now, I do not know if Kithless or Seemingless were official thing in 1ed, but I recall seeing those on this forum. Or maybe I read about &quot;Keeper-less&quot; in Hegde chapter of 1ed corebook few days ago? I maybe wrting stupids, mark me, but I thing interesting would be thinking about them even in context of 2ed.<br /> <br /> So, to clarify once and for all - there is not any possibility, officially, for mortal to become a changeling without a True Fae taking a role of Keeper for her.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-18T23:47:51-08:00","id":344438,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BrilliantRain</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/341562-preliminary-outline-for-changeling-the-lost-second-edition?p=344403#post344403\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I missed the outline, so perhaps someone can tell me if pulling a Snow White is an option? I mean, giving the fairy tale themes that crop up in Changeling, the first thing I imagined when I heard the Huntsmen was the guy from Snow White who tells the Queen he's killed the Princess, but really didn't. I presume there's a section on escaping the huntsmen, but I'm curious if enticing/suborning/tricking/or otherwise manipulating the Huntsmen is possible (since I don't actually even know what they are).</div> </div> </div> </div>It didn't say one way or the other. I think it's a good idea.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I call the Integrity-analogue the &quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/822559-trying-to-understand-the-morality-system?p=825008#post825008\" target=\"_blank\">subjective stat</a>&quot;.<br /> An explanation how to <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/913221-using-social-manuevering\" target=\"_blank\">use Social Manuevering</a>.<br /> Guanxi Explanations: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=787824#post787824\" target=\"_blank\">1</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=788173#post788173\" target=\"_blank\">2</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/833863-mages-and-trading-favors?p=834531#post834531\" target=\"_blank\">3</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2758-errol216","name":"Errol216","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-18T23:48:56-08:00","id":344439,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/341562-preliminary-outline-for-changeling-the-lost-second-edition?p=344429#post344429\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As I only reread corebook now, I do not know if Kithless or Seemingless were official thing in 1ed, but I recall seeing those on this forum.</div> </div> </div> </div>Kithless was possible from the start in 1e (the three seemings with the fewest core kiths had the highest implied proportion of kithless). Not having a seeming didn't show up until Equinox Road, where it was part of a more graduated scale of transformation.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> So, to clarify once and for all - there is not any possibility, officially, for mortal to become a changeling without a True Fae taking a role of Keeper for her. </div> </div> </div>The metaphysics of Faerie prevent it from providing succor to anything that doesn't have an agreement with it - and the Fae <i>are </i>Faerie. Likewise, agreements aren't always explicitly agreements; to borrow an example, an impromptu fight over a possession is an agreement between two parties - if your opponent abandons the fight, you as the challenger can't actually win.<br /> <br /> Similarly, accepting succor is tacit acceptance of the bonds of hospitality - you can wander in an &quot;abandoned&quot; Fae domain for years scrounging leftovers and never encounter any signatory to the laws that prevent Arcadia from simply withholding sustenance, but the fact that you found food and it didn't <i>not</i> feed you means something was making you an offer and you took it.<br /> <br /> The Shadow and the Lord are Fae archetypes for a reason, too - some of the Strangers will just cut you a deal and turn you loose on their mansion-grounds or toss you in the attic and forget about you for a decade.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":111,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","user":"Satchel","date":". 12-19-2014, 02:51 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-19T04:43:12-08:00","id":344562,"title":"","content":"Like many things faerie, sometimes the symbolism of an act is closer to the truth of things than the act itself. It's also very much a &quot;Fruit of the Underworld&quot; concept, which you can find in several mythos throughout. Someone ends up in the underworld, throught fortune, design, or the natural way of things. To survive there or be allowed to leave, they must partake of its food, an act which forever binds them to it in some way.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","name":"YeOfLittleFaith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar188_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-19T06:06:25-08:00","id":344605,"title":"","content":"Surviving on your own in Arcadian realm can mean that you unknowingly or knowingly struck deals with the Realm form of the Fae and the Fae in question does not care about ruling over those Changelings. It may derive substinence from watching Changelings argue over limited resources in the Realm and/or be harsh but survivable to generate conflict in such way. Changelings are 'free' in the sense that there is no visible presence that rules over them, but the hell is other people. The Fae is just vicariously watching.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cI am absolute, I am perfect, I am supreme. I shall be eternal. My tragedy, is that there is no other fate for me. My powerlessness was that I couldn\u2019t subjugate my journey to the gods, while dreaming of rebirth at the end of distant time, like other pharaohs.\u201d Ramesses II, Fate/Prototype: Argent Fragments.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2918-kat","name":"Kat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2918_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1762"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-19T12:21:15-08:00","id":345025,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MachineIV</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/341562-preliminary-outline-for-changeling-the-lost-second-edition?p=342352#post342352\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just an FYI, I'm pulling the link at request while it gets reviewed. I'll try to address the stuff that was brought up, particularly in Gaius's comments there. It's mostly just stuff that slipped my mind. But, that's why I posted it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ahh, makes sense to me. Thanks for clarifying. I'm very unfamiliar with the process; I'd presumed this was &quot;the final version of the outline, pending approval,&quot; but it sounds more like this is a draft on which you intend to get official feedback, as well as feedback and thoughts from the forums. Am I close?<br /> <br /> Having thought a few days on this, I'm interested in icons. It seems like a cool idea, and not just for building off the &quot;personal myth&quot; idea that I'm also really digging. The thought of little bits that tore off of the Changeling in the Hedge forming into ties to that Changeling's legend is very cool, and an appropriate means of tracking the Lost. I wonder what other properties they might have and what other uses they might serve.<br /> <br /> That said, I do admit to having a possibly unfounded concern about their property of forever reappearing in the Hedge. Some executions of that idea with the Huntsmen could tip the tone from &quot;I can never know if I'm safe,&quot; to &quot;I know I'm never safe.&quot; Not jumping to conclusions here, just mentioning initial thoughts that strike me from the exceptionally little that's yet been mentioned.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-19T12:53:11-08:00","id":345054,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/341562-preliminary-outline-for-changeling-the-lost-second-edition?p=344439#post344439\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The metaphysics of Faerie prevent it from providing succor to anything that doesn't have an agreement with it - and the Fae <i>are </i>Faerie. Likewise, agreements aren't always explicitly agreements; to borrow an example, an impromptu fight over a possession is an agreement between two parties - if your opponent abandons the fight, you as the challenger can't actually win.<br /> <br /> Similarly, accepting succor is tacit acceptance of the bonds of hospitality - you can wander in an &quot;abandoned&quot; Fae domain for years scrounging leftovers and never encounter any signatory to the laws that prevent Arcadia from simply withholding sustenance, but the fact that you found food and it didn't <i>not</i> feed you means something was making you an offer and you took it.<br /> <br /> The Shadow and the Lord are Fae archetypes for a reason, too - some of the Strangers will just cut you a deal and turn you loose on their mansion-grounds or toss you in the attic and forget about you for a decade.</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay. with having this in mind, how to make a 2ed Kithless and Seemingless work? If Kiths are role you played in Arcadia, even if no Fae made you do his will, what are Kithless? Those that only gone to Faerie to run from it with Contract signed with it and been &quot;free&quot; by Seeming means?<br /> <br /> And the other way around - are those that are Seemingless now, with Seemings being ways you freed yourself from Arcadia, are those that were left behind? You could not now play a Seemingless the Lost, as those are in Faerie for all eternity, working for Gentry?<br /> <br /> To be frank, even if I generally like the Kiths being represented in all Seemings, I have above problems with &quot;Seemings as a way out of Arcadia&quot; interpretation now 2ed is heading. I would more be in favor that Seemings are not &quot;a story of mine return&quot;, but rather &quot;a story of mine Durance&quot;, like in 1ed they were. Because not every Kithless left Arcadia - with now propositon for 2ed they would be both Kithless and Seemingless, as they were not free.<br /> <br /> Being Darkling is not about &quot;I was ruthless in Fearie and so it free me&quot;, it's more with &quot;I like darkness and decivness because mine Durance was that&quot;. More a &quot;personality scary&quot; than &quot;way out of Arcadia&quot;.<br /> <br /> This would easily solve out Kithless problem - those changelings that are in Arcadia just relive thur Durance still, and Seeming it's not a &quot;story of our escape&quot;, but rather &quot;a story of our Durance&quot;. The matter that most Fairest use they charms, and Beast their instincts to escape, is just another implication of this, not main tone.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 12-19-2014, 03:57 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-19T13:34:59-08:00","id":345103,"title":"","content":"For one I prefer approach of 2nd edition. The escape is as important part of Changeling's existence as their Durance which is easily symbolized by their Kith. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Okay. with having this in mind, how to make a 2ed Kithless and Seemingless work? If Kiths are role you played in Arcadia, even if no Fae made you do his will, what are Kithless? Those that only gone to Faerie to run from it with Contract signed with it and been &quot;free&quot; by Seeming means?<br /> <br /> And the other way around - are those that are Seemingless now, with Seemings being ways you freed yourself from Arcadia, are those that were left behind? You could not now play a Seemingless the Lost, as those are in Faerie for all eternity, working for Gentry? </div> </div> </div>If those two are problematic in the context of 2ed then they should be rid of.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cI am absolute, I am perfect, I am supreme. I shall be eternal. My tragedy, is that there is no other fate for me. My powerlessness was that I couldn\u2019t subjugate my journey to the gods, while dreaming of rebirth at the end of distant time, like other pharaohs.\u201d Ramesses II, Fate/Prototype: Argent Fragments.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2918-kat","name":"Kat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2918_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1762"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-19T17:22:05-08:00","id":345273,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kat</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/341562-preliminary-outline-for-changeling-the-lost-second-edition?p=345103#post345103\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For one I prefer approach of 2nd edition. The escape is as important part of Changeling's existence as their Durance which is easily symbolized by their Kith.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> If those two are problematic in the context of 2ed then they should be rid of.</div> </div> </div> </div>Characters with no Seeming work fine in 2e so far. I don't think I'd use kithless characters. Seemingless characters might result from dumb luck, or a sufficiently diverse escape that it didn't define you any which way. But I think they should be exceedingly rare, since it's an identifying trait.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-19T18:16:47-08:00","id":345288,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> sufficiently diverse escape that it didn't define you any which way </div> </div> </div>So, how the lack of Seeming could impact the character mechanically if he was 'Jack of all trades' in his approach to escaping Durance? I'm curious about that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cI am absolute, I am perfect, I am supreme. I shall be eternal. My tragedy, is that there is no other fate for me. My powerlessness was that I couldn\u2019t subjugate my journey to the gods, while dreaming of rebirth at the end of distant time, like other pharaohs.\u201d Ramesses II, Fate/Prototype: Argent Fragments.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2918-kat","name":"Kat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2918_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1762"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-19T18:17:04-08:00","id":345289,"title":"","content":"I'm curious about the &quot;small rituals&quot; that changelings perform. I don't recall the exact wording, though I do recall in the doc that they can keep the huntsmen at bay, and also an amusing line about looking like a jackass skipping rope in public. Could you possibly expand on these rituals at all? Are they &quot;step on a crack, break your mother's back&quot; type things?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1423-espritdecalmar","name":"espritdecalmar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1423_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-19T20:42:11-08:00","id":345372,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>espritdecalmar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/341562-preliminary-outline-for-changeling-the-lost-second-edition?p=345289#post345289\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm curious about the &quot;small rituals&quot; that changelings perform. I don't recall the exact wording, though I do recall in the doc that they can keep the huntsmen at bay, and also an amusing line about looking like a jackass skipping rope in public. Could you possibly expand on these rituals at all? Are they &quot;step on a crack, break your mother's back&quot; type things?</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't have it in front of me, but I think that section spoke of the rituals casting off the lies of the mask for the Changeling (which Changelings in general found a very gauche thing to do). There was some implication that either this same sort of ritual or something like it couldn't keep the huntsmen at bay, but might throw off their own &quot;look like anything&quot; deceptions.<br /> <br /> I'm interested in the answer to espiritedcalmar's question. Also, because of how my mind works, whether that amusing line meant a) the Changeling looks like a jerk doing something childish, b) the Changeling looks as ridiculous as an actual donkey skipping rope, c) (super literal option) a donkey-like Changeling who decided to skip rope would look exactly like that upon using the ceremony, and/or something else. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-20T00:05:57-08:00","id":345500,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>espritdecalmar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/341562-preliminary-outline-for-changeling-the-lost-second-edition?p=345289#post345289\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm curious about the &quot;small rituals&quot; that changelings perform. I don't recall the exact wording, though I do recall in the doc that they can keep the huntsmen at bay, and also an amusing line about looking like a jackass skipping rope in public. Could you possibly expand on these rituals at all? Are they &quot;step on a crack, break your mother's back&quot; type things?</div> </div> </div> </div>Leave milk out for the elves, or they steal your children away...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/209-that-other-guy","name":"That Other Guy","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"702"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-20T01:41:50-08:00","id":345555,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MachineIV</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/341562-preliminary-outline-for-changeling-the-lost-second-edition?p=345273#post345273\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Characters with no Seeming work fine in 2e so far. I don't think I'd use kithless characters. Seemingless characters might result from dumb luck, or a sufficiently diverse escape that it didn't define you any which way. But I think they should be exceedingly rare, since it's an identifying trait.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd also play up paranoia around a Changeling with no Seeming, whether it was warranted or not; much more likely to be thought a loyalist, with the lack of Seeming being because you never did break free. That'd be a powerful prejudice to have to fight against if you *aren't* a loyalist, which could lead to some very interesting complications for taking that option.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/614-eolirin","name":"Eolirin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-20T03:03:56-08:00","id":345606,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kat</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/341562-preliminary-outline-for-changeling-the-lost-second-edition?p=345103#post345103\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For one I prefer approach of 2nd edition. The escape is as important part of Changeling's existence as their Durance which is easily symbolized by their Kith.</div> </div> </div> </div>But the logical implications of Gentry stealing mortals to become changelings, is that not all of them escape. Some are in Arcadia, not freed from the slavery of Fae. They would still have Kiths ( as the are remade by Others to fulfill their role in Faerie ) but they never get Seemings in 2ed way, as they <b>never</b> been free, still being in Arcadia. So, going with this, Loyalist will be Seemingless, or they will have Seemings? They never truly left their Keepers, isn't they?<br /> <br /> As to Kithless - so you are random mortal that got to Arcadia, sign some Contracts, and run before forming Kith? With Seeming left on you by your escape?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kat</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/341562-preliminary-outline-for-changeling-the-lost-second-edition?p=345103#post345103\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If those two are problematic in the context of 2ed then they should be rid of.</div> </div> </div> </div>If you get rid of them, there always will be players that will see there is illogical gap in setting, breaking immersion. Better is to think of this scenario <b>before</b> writing 2ed Kiths and Seemings. It's exactly why this topic was made by <b>DavidH.</b>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-20T03:49:47-08:00","id":345668,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> But the logical implications of Gentry stealing mortals to become changelings, is that not all of them escape. Some are in Arcadia, not freed from the slavery of Fae. They would still have Kiths ( as the are remade by Others to fulfill their role in Faerie ) but they never get Seemings in 2ed way, as they <b>never</b> been free, still being in Arcadia. So, going with this, Loyalist will be Seemingless, or they will have Seemings? They never truly left their Keepers, isn't they? </div> </div> </div>So, suddenly being kithless makes a changeling suspect of being a Loyalist in the eyes of the Courts?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2411-raistlin","name":"Raistlin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"713"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-20T04:13:19-08:00","id":345670,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Raistlin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/341562-preliminary-outline-for-changeling-the-lost-second-edition?p=345668#post345668\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So, suddenly being kithless makes a changeling suspect of being a Loyalist in the eyes of the Courts?</div> </div> </div> </div>Rather Seemingless, because the Seeming is decidng that you run from your Keeper in 2ed, is it not? So Seemingless changleings should be watched as probable Loyalist, not freed from their Lords.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-20T05:05:05-08:00","id":345682,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If you get rid of them, there always will be players that will see there is illogical gap in setting, breaking immersion. Better is to think of this scenario before writing 2ed Kiths and Seemings. It's exactly why this topic was made by DavidH. </div> </div> </div>If kithless and seemingless Changelings are disposed of, or they are ultimately modelled in vastly different way, it's good to remind it's 2ed after all, meant by default to be different from 1ed. Let's face it, you cannot make everyone happy even with writers here making sure they have feedback from the community. Even if some things from 1ed I do like are cut out or changed in different form, it does not matter to me since I will judge 2ed and 1ed as seperate editions. So far, I like many changes implied for 2ed, so I guess I will stay loyal to both.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cI am absolute, I am perfect, I am supreme. I shall be eternal. My tragedy, is that there is no other fate for me. My powerlessness was that I couldn\u2019t subjugate my journey to the gods, while dreaming of rebirth at the end of distant time, like other pharaohs.\u201d Ramesses II, Fate/Prototype: Argent Fragments.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2918-kat","name":"Kat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2918_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1762"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-20T05:14:28-08:00","id":345685,"title":"","content":"Or we could make changes that way as make as small difference in 1ed material - like making Kithless and Seemingless still viable, just remembering setting implications of them. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-20T05:43:28-08:00","id":345692,"title":"","content":"Given Contracts and Seemings/Kith system are already IMO a major change from 1ed's system, it's already different edition in alpha stage. Any element should be internally consistent within 2ed's framework, priority given to that over consistency with previous editions.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cI am absolute, I am perfect, I am supreme. I shall be eternal. My tragedy, is that there is no other fate for me. My powerlessness was that I couldn\u2019t subjugate my journey to the gods, while dreaming of rebirth at the end of distant time, like other pharaohs.\u201d Ramesses II, Fate/Prototype: Argent Fragments.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2918-kat","name":"Kat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2918_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1762"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-20T06:30:13-08:00","id":345724,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>espritdecalmar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/341562-preliminary-outline-for-changeling-the-lost-second-edition?p=345289#post345289\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm curious about the &quot;small rituals&quot; that changelings perform. I don't recall the exact wording, though I do recall in the doc that they can keep the huntsmen at bay, and also an amusing line about looking like a jackass skipping rope in public. Could you possibly expand on these rituals at all? Are they &quot;step on a crack, break your mother's back&quot; type things?</div> </div> </div> </div>Basically, it's something you carried forward from your durance. You play that part just enough to draw Arcadia close, and because reality doesn't like that, it whips back a little, pulling other masks with it. It's the metaphysical equivalent of breaking suspension of disbelief.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-20T06:30:45-08:00","id":345725,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Raistlin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/341562-preliminary-outline-for-changeling-the-lost-second-edition?p=345668#post345668\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So, suddenly being kithless makes a changeling suspect of being a Loyalist in the eyes of the Courts?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think that'd be the obvious way to look at them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-20T08:24:29-08:00","id":345782,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MachineIV</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/341562-preliminary-outline-for-changeling-the-lost-second-edition?p=345724#post345724\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Basically, it's something you carried forward from your durance. You play that part just enough to draw Arcadia close, and because reality doesn't like that, it whips back a little, pulling other masks with it. It's the metaphysical equivalent of breaking suspension of disbelief.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's interesting. So, if you were a shark in Faerie, by acting shark-like on Earth, you confuse reality? Which also makes it sound like the nature of the Mask is being altered a little, like with the mirror thing in <i>Blood &amp; Smoke</i>.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1423-espritdecalmar","name":"espritdecalmar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1423_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-20T16:21:11-08:00","id":346227,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>espritdecalmar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/341562-preliminary-outline-for-changeling-the-lost-second-edition?p=345782#post345782\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's interesting. So, if you were a shark in Faerie, by acting shark-like on Earth, you confuse reality? Which also makes it sound like the nature of the Mask is being altered a little, like with the mirror thing in <i>Blood &amp; Smoke</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah. There's going to be some subtle differences. But not the kind of stuff I can talk about yet, because it's going to depend on how whomever writes it feels it out in the process, and how I like that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-20T20:13:03-08:00","id":346367,"title":"","content":"Huntsmen sound like a plot tumor just waiting to go malignant and their whole &quot;they can be anything even a toaster!&quot; schtick comes off more silly than scary. Everything else looks fairly promising.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/218-two-shadows","name":"Two-Shadows","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar218_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"65"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-20T21:33:47-08:00","id":346447,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Two-Shadows</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/341562-preliminary-outline-for-changeling-the-lost-second-edition?p=346367#post346367\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Huntsmen sound like a plot tumor just waiting to go malignant and their whole &quot;they can be anything even a toaster!&quot; schtick comes off more silly than scary. Everything else looks fairly promising.</div> </div> </div> </div>In fairness, I read that line as more having some playful fun with a topic; an entity that can be literally anything or anyone has so many obvious ways it can be menacing. That said, I'm also waiting to hear more and/or see the execution. As they're giving some sample huntsmen, it sounds like each is an individual, with its own proclivities, defining powers and strategies, etc. even if super-potent control of their masks is a given. I'm interested to hear more about them; as long as each huntsman doesn't feel completely-to-mostly interchangeable with any others, there's potential.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-21T02:57:57-08:00","id":346558,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Two-Shadows</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/341562-preliminary-outline-for-changeling-the-lost-second-edition?p=346367#post346367\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Huntsmen sound like a plot tumor just waiting to go malignant and their whole &quot;they can be anything even a toaster!&quot; schtick comes off more silly than scary. Everything else looks fairly promising.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah. I'm sorry. I try to keep my outlines lighthearted. I figure any of my writers get that I don't want them to actually say that. <br /> <br /> Guess that can be a problem with open development.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-21T04:37:02-08:00","id":346583,"title":"","content":"IMO Huntsmen will warrant a separate open development thread at some point, just saying. It's enough major addition to dedicate a one to.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cI am absolute, I am perfect, I am supreme. I shall be eternal. My tragedy, is that there is no other fate for me. My powerlessness was that I couldn\u2019t subjugate my journey to the gods, while dreaming of rebirth at the end of distant time, like other pharaohs.\u201d Ramesses II, Fate/Prototype: Argent Fragments.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2918-kat","name":"Kat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2918_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1762"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-21T06:00:14-08:00","id":346593,"title":"","content":"Errrrr, what did I miss? The thread is called &quot;Preliminary Outline for Changeling: The Lost Second Edition&quot;, and you keep talking about it, but I don't see the outline in question. Can someone provide a link?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/216-zooroos","name":"Zooroos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar216_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"250"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-21T06:23:24-08:00","id":346597,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Errrrr, what did I miss? The thread is called &quot;Preliminary Outline for Changeling: The Lost Second Edition&quot;, and you keep talking about it, but I don't see the outline in question. Can someone provide a link? </div> </div> </div>It got removed for time being, so it is not at Google Docs anymore. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cI am absolute, I am perfect, I am supreme. I shall be eternal. My tragedy, is that there is no other fate for me. My powerlessness was that I couldn\u2019t subjugate my journey to the gods, while dreaming of rebirth at the end of distant time, like other pharaohs.\u201d Ramesses II, Fate/Prototype: Argent Fragments.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2918-kat","name":"Kat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2918_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1762"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-21T11:59:43-08:00","id":346869,"title":"","content":"I could see Hunters as being Goblins, Hobgoblins, Fetches, Pacted humans *and* Changelings. Any given Hunter pack could be made of a mix of any of them - though some will be rarer than others.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.dropbox.com/s/ofii86boiyk38ng/DtDRandomForms.zip\" target=\"_blank\">Open the gates of Hell: Random Demon Generator.</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1X6qQzoAPrSRNzl3cQcMWasoPv3eK56sIlAOTeay61No/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Gather an army of Rage! Random Garou Generator.</a><br /> Shapeshifting Historian<br /> Writer - Werewolf: the Apocalypse, Werewolf: the Forsaken, Exalted 3e, TC: \u00c6on","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/167-nikink","name":"nikink","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"360"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-21T13:26:17-08:00","id":346931,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MachineIV</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/341562-preliminary-outline-for-changeling-the-lost-second-edition?p=346558#post346558\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah. I'm sorry. I try to keep my outlines lighthearted. I figure any of my writers get that I don't want them to actually say that.<br /> <br /> Guess that can be a problem with open development.</div> </div> </div> </div>My misinterpretation is on me, not you.<br /> <br /> I still worry about the huntsmen's potential for hijacking/derailing a game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/218-two-shadows","name":"Two-Shadows","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar218_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"65"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-21T13:36:38-08:00","id":346947,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Two-Shadows</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/341562-preliminary-outline-for-changeling-the-lost-second-edition?p=346931#post346931\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> My misinterpretation is on me, not you.<br /> <br /> I still worry about the huntsmen's potential for hijacking/derailing a game.</div> </div> </div> </div>You're not alone in that. Personally, I think it's an idea that needs expansion, I just see how it can be expanded to avoid becoming too much of a spotlight hog.<br /> <br /> I will say that True Fae not hogging as much is probably a good thing overall, I got sick of Fae as Pyramid Head, every time they showed up.<br /> <br /> They're supposed to be more mysterious and powerful than that, even if they're very personal tormentors. Again, could help show how the Court System actually does keep them away.<br /> <br /> Hey, here's a thought-some Huntsmen are just as much victims of the True Fae as their quarry is, but they don't really have a choice. Also, their Ban equivalent is the circumstance where they may actually abduct someone, otherwise they're under Wyrd law to avoid directly attacking, though not harassment. This is generally a state that isolates the prey in some fashion, whether they be oathbreakers, motley-less, or lack a human identity. <br /> <br /> I'd also recommend to avoid them being one-trick ponies; they hunt, but they don't necessarily hunt for changelings, although that's a big percentage of their paycheck. Many are on other errands in the mortal world for True Fae, or even between jobs and using their abilities in the mortal world for their own agenda.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-21T14:50:16-08:00","id":347009,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leliel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/341562-preliminary-outline-for-changeling-the-lost-second-edition?p=346947#post346947\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'd also recommend to avoid them being one-trick ponies; they hunt, but they don't necessarily hunt for changelings, although that's a big percentage of their paycheck. Many are on other errands in the mortal world for True Fae, or even between jobs and using their abilities in the mortal world for their own agenda.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is a topic I want to see addressed. I figure the &quot;big name&quot; Huntsmen focus exclusively on Changelings, because they have the reputation to get those gigs. But that's not all of them, all of the time. In the real world, bail bondsmen often spend time doing low level PI work as well. I figure Huntsmen aren't dissimilar.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-21T15:02:22-08:00","id":347015,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leliel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/341562-preliminary-outline-for-changeling-the-lost-second-edition?p=346947#post346947\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hey, here's a thought-some Huntsmen are just as much victims of the True Fae as their quarry is, but they don't really have a choice. Also, their Ban equivalent is the circumstance where they may actually abduct someone, otherwise they're under Wyrd law to avoid directly attacking, though not harassment. This is generally a state that isolates the prey in some fashion, whether they be oathbreakers, motley-less, or lack a human identity.</div> </div> </div> </div> Personally I'd tie that to the Courts. Each Court sets the rules by which the Huntsmen can hunt it's members.<br /> <br /> Using my Flower Courts as an example (or Spring, though I would never suggest this for Autumn or Winter).<br /> <br /> 1) Huntsmen must disguise themselves as a mortal while within freehold territory.<br /> 2) Huntsmen must avoid all contact with the mortal they are disguised as.<br /> 3) Huntsmen must obey all Pledges signed by the mortal they are desguised as; Huntsmen are entitled to know the details of all Pledges before committing to a disguise.<br /> <br /> It seems like a very faeish way to approach the problem of being hunted; and it can also be a great way to strengthen the abuse survivor theme. Those rules above encourage changelings to go out and make lots of connections and pledges with people, because people with Pledges are safe. I admit though, it might encourage a hyperfocus on anti-huntsmen Pledges.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":134,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","user":"The Kings Raven","date":". 12-21-2014, 06:07 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-21T15:03:11-08:00","id":347016,"title":"","content":"Is there a crossover potential for Huntsmen, if they don't necessarily hunt Changelings, at least those who are not top in their 'trade'?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cI am absolute, I am perfect, I am supreme. I shall be eternal. My tragedy, is that there is no other fate for me. My powerlessness was that I couldn\u2019t subjugate my journey to the gods, while dreaming of rebirth at the end of distant time, like other pharaohs.\u201d Ramesses II, Fate/Prototype: Argent Fragments.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2918-kat","name":"Kat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2918_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1762"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-21T16:52:27-08:00","id":347068,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kat</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/341562-preliminary-outline-for-changeling-the-lost-second-edition?p=347016#post347016\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is there a crossover potential for Huntsmen, if they don't necessarily hunt Changelings, at least those who are not top in their 'trade'?</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't know if we'll have room to talk about it. But I don't see why not.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-22T06:56:54-08:00","id":347365,"title":"","content":"I wonder if it's a source of angst for some changelings out there that their Keepers don't care enough to hunt down their old charges themselves. Even for the ones who are adamant about never going back, I imagine this moment of shock and disbelief at the idea of being hunted down by a middleman, when the original kidnapper went through so much personal effort to catch and confine the changeling in question.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1423-espritdecalmar","name":"espritdecalmar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1423_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-22T07:10:13-08:00","id":347367,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I wonder if it's a source of angst for some changelings out there that their Keepers don't care enough to hunt down their old charges themselves. Even for the ones who are adamant about never going back, I imagine this moment of shock and disbelief at the idea of being hunted down by a middleman, when the original kidnapper went through so much personal effort to catch and confine the changeling in question. </div> </div> </div>My 1ed Changeling would feel offended because she wants to kill the Keeper as one of her long term goals.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cI am absolute, I am perfect, I am supreme. I shall be eternal. My tragedy, is that there is no other fate for me. My powerlessness was that I couldn\u2019t subjugate my journey to the gods, while dreaming of rebirth at the end of distant time, like other pharaohs.\u201d Ramesses II, Fate/Prototype: Argent Fragments.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2918-kat","name":"Kat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2918_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1762"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-22T12:56:32-08:00","id":347612,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kat</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/341562-preliminary-outline-for-changeling-the-lost-second-edition?p=347016#post347016\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is there a crossover potential for Huntsmen, if they don't necessarily hunt Changelings, at least those who are not top in their 'trade'?</div> </div> </div> </div>I can definately see that. Though i can see the Hunstman go for &quot;quality&quot; targets other supernaturals to Hunters than every day mortals.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><i>&quot;I am a daydreamer and a Night thinker.&quot;~</i></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1820-nightout","name":"Nightout","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1820_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"57"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-22T17:46:46-08:00","id":347881,"title":"","content":"I'd actually like to see expansion of the social maneuvering rules and how they can be applied to True Fae. I think that, generally, the Others shouldn't be a threat that you fight, but can be one that you can fool, trick, distract, and outmaneuver, particularly by taking advantage of their bans and blind spots. I think this really needs its own section in the book. I mean, the Court system is a perfect example of using their prejudices against them (voluntary surrender of power and fixed seasonal cycle being things they have trouble grasping).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Eric Christian Berg</b><br /> <i>Onyx Path Freelancer</i><br /> Promethean: The Created Second Edition, Dark Eras Companion","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2019-eberg","name":"eberg","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2019_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"284"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-22T18:28:16-08:00","id":347924,"title":"","content":"Absolutely seconded; this is practically a defining element in folklore. The Others are powerful and terrible and mighty, but they're also defined by their natures. They can quite often be cocky, bored, vice-ridden, or otherwise manipulable by some feature of their mental anatomy. Might be handy to have some feature to them that makes it easier to manipulate them by these elements of their natures. Perhaps Redtooth-Redtooth can be placated by feeding him something (or someone) delectable? Or he can be tricked into stopping (and losing precious time in the material world) - or at least delayed - by promising a sumptuous meal?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-22T20:25:39-08:00","id":347963,"title":"","content":"I always dug in Nobilis that you could mess with those who followed the Code of the Wild by giving them something. Their sense of obligation put them in debt to you.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Eric Christian Berg</b><br /> <i>Onyx Path Freelancer</i><br /> Promethean: The Created Second Edition, Dark Eras Companion","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2019-eberg","name":"eberg","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2019_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"284"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-22T20:40:06-08:00","id":347971,"title":"","content":"Of course, having one of the Others in your debt is nearly as dangerous as being in debt to one of the Others...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1168-hobbitguy1420","name":"HobbitGuy1420","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"332"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-23T14:36:13-08:00","id":348556,"title":"","content":"Quite true. But wouldn't want things to be dull. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Eric Christian Berg</b><br /> <i>Onyx Path Freelancer</i><br /> Promethean: The Created Second Edition, Dark Eras Companion","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2019-eberg","name":"eberg","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2019_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"284"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-23T14:51:56-08:00","id":348558,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>eberg</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/341562-preliminary-outline-for-changeling-the-lost-second-edition?p=348556#post348556\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Quite true. But wouldn't want things to be dull. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Hunh, on a possibly related note, it just struck me that we're lacking in details about how Clarity's planned to work in 2e. It's got some discussion on the mailing list, it seems, but that's it. I wonder how different it might wind up being...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-23T16:25:27-08:00","id":348615,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>eberg</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/341562-preliminary-outline-for-changeling-the-lost-second-edition?p=347881#post347881\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd actually like to see expansion of the social maneuvering rules and how they can be applied to True Fae. I think that, generally, the Others shouldn't be a threat that you fight, but can be one that you can fool, trick, distract, and outmaneuver, particularly by taking advantage of their bans and blind spots. I think this really needs its own section in the book. I mean, the Court system is a perfect example of using their prejudices against them (voluntary surrender of power and fixed seasonal cycle being things they have trouble grasping).</div> </div> </div> </div>I really like this idea. I'll talk to whomever I have doing the Storytelling chapter about it. So far, I've ended up doing most of the Storytelling chapters, or Filamena did. So they've always been a place I love seeing fun experimentation like that. I dig.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-23T22:44:37-08:00","id":348823,"title":"","content":"Question that come out when I analyzed the <i>Books of Faerie</i> as inspiration for <b>Changeling</b> - <br /> <br /> What about Seemings for the True Fae? Because the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/348801-the-books-of-faerie-inspirations?p=348822#post348822\">Auberon and Titania are both very much Fae and perfect examples of Fairest Seeming</a>. But with the Seeming becoming defining the &quot;way out of Faerie&quot; , I see this being a bit hard to reconcile now.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-24T04:46:23-08:00","id":348944,"title":"","content":"No, they should not have Seemings going by 2ed logic because Seemings represent how Changelings escaped their Durance.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cI am absolute, I am perfect, I am supreme. I shall be eternal. My tragedy, is that there is no other fate for me. My powerlessness was that I couldn\u2019t subjugate my journey to the gods, while dreaming of rebirth at the end of distant time, like other pharaohs.\u201d Ramesses II, Fate/Prototype: Argent Fragments.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2918-kat","name":"Kat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2918_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1762"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-24T05:07:50-08:00","id":348968,"title":"","content":"Did Fae even have Seemings in 1e? I have this vague memory that they didn't exactly, although they could manifest similar powers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-24T05:26:50-08:00","id":348980,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Did Fae even have Seemings in 1e? I have this vague memory that they didn't exactly, although they could manifest similar powers. </div> </div> </div>They could have for their Actor forms as far as I remember, but it was a matter of a whim.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cI am absolute, I am perfect, I am supreme. I shall be eternal. My tragedy, is that there is no other fate for me. My powerlessness was that I couldn\u2019t subjugate my journey to the gods, while dreaming of rebirth at the end of distant time, like other pharaohs.\u201d Ramesses II, Fate/Prototype: Argent Fragments.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2918-kat","name":"Kat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2918_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1762"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-24T06:19:19-08:00","id":348992,"title":"","content":"In Autumn Nightmares they could have a number of mien blessings that replicated Seeming and Kith blessings or unique ones. If they really wanted to, I don't see why they couldn't still have them in 2e, but there is a much greater symbolism in the Seemings for the changeling, so I guess it depends.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","name":"YeOfLittleFaith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar188_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-24T06:20:15-08:00","id":348993,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/341562-preliminary-outline-for-changeling-the-lost-second-edition?p=347015#post347015\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Personally I'd tie that to the Courts. Each Court sets the rules by which the Huntsmen can hunt it's members.<br /> <br /> Using my Flower Courts as an example (or Spring, though I would never suggest this for Autumn or Winter).<br /> <br /> 1) Huntsmen must disguise themselves as a mortal while within freehold territory.<br /> 2) Huntsmen must avoid all contact with the mortal they are disguised as.<br /> 3) Huntsmen must obey all Pledges signed by the mortal they are desguised as; Huntsmen are entitled to know the details of all Pledges before committing to a disguise.<br /> <br /> It seems like a very faeish way to approach the problem of being hunted; and it can also be a great way to strengthen the abuse survivor theme. Those rules above encourage changelings to go out and make lots of connections and pledges with people, because people with Pledges are safe. I admit though, it might encourage a hyperfocus on anti-huntsmen Pledges.</div> </div> </div> </div>This post made me realize a couple of things that I think kinda turned me off to 1e.<br /> <br /> 1) I never really got why the whole Court system was supposed to keep you safe from the Keepers. So, having something like this, where your Court directly controls how you can be hunted would be an improvement in helping me, at least, get how being in a Court is a good thing and why you can't just go find a job somewhere else and pretend like none of this ever happened.<br /> <br /> 2) I didn't really like any of the courts. It's been long enough that I don't really remember why, but none of them floated my boat. I'll have to look over my book and see if I can figure out why, so I can give proper feedback, but I was curious if anyone else had felt that way.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-24T07:47:20-08:00","id":349054,"title":"","content":"First off, better organised Changelings can put up more fight against any incursion from Arcadia/Hedge, and the concept of shifting seasons and change in authority depending on the season in question is something True Fae have it hard to grasp, so that gives some protection against their intrigues.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cI am absolute, I am perfect, I am supreme. I shall be eternal. My tragedy, is that there is no other fate for me. My powerlessness was that I couldn\u2019t subjugate my journey to the gods, while dreaming of rebirth at the end of distant time, like other pharaohs.\u201d Ramesses II, Fate/Prototype: Argent Fragments.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2918-kat","name":"Kat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2918_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1762"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-24T09:01:26-08:00","id":349070,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kat</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/341562-preliminary-outline-for-changeling-the-lost-second-edition?p=349054#post349054\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">First off, better organised Changelings can put up more fight against any incursion from Arcadia/Hedge, and the concept of shifting seasons and change in authority depending on the season in question is something True Fae have it hard to grasp, so that gives some protection against their intrigues.</div> </div> </div> </div>I thought a bigger part of it was not so much changing with the seasons, but of each court voluntarily ceding authority to another, which baffles the True Fae. In hindsight, this felt for a moment like it didn't jive very well with the depiction the Others ultimately got, but I think it still does. I mean, a True Fae can theoretically be as powerful as it wants to be, but it won't get any of the sort of conflict it needs to survive if it does that, so it has to deliberately make itself such that opposing and even defeating it is possible. The Strangers thus know what it is to limit themselves toward the antagonistic end of creating conflict, but don't comprehend the notion of Changelings cooperatively limiting themselves to the end of (in principle) <i>reducing</i> conflict, as they do when voluntarily handing off ruling power to another.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-24T09:21:51-08:00","id":349100,"title":"","content":"That's what I meant by changes in authority.<br /> <br /> Also True Fae are not that powerful on Ironside, being limited to permament trait cap of 6, so no wonder why they reluctantly travel there even with clear objective.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cI am absolute, I am perfect, I am supreme. I shall be eternal. My tragedy, is that there is no other fate for me. My powerlessness was that I couldn\u2019t subjugate my journey to the gods, while dreaming of rebirth at the end of distant time, like other pharaohs.\u201d Ramesses II, Fate/Prototype: Argent Fragments.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2918-kat","name":"Kat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2918_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1762"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-25T03:33:39-08:00","id":349734,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>eberg</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/341562-preliminary-outline-for-changeling-the-lost-second-edition?p=347881#post347881\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd actually like to see expansion of the social maneuvering rules and how they can be applied to True Fae. I think that, generally, the Others shouldn't be a threat that you fight, but can be one that you can fool, trick, distract, and outmaneuver, particularly by taking advantage of their bans and blind spots. I think this really needs its own section in the book. I mean, the Court system is a perfect example of using their prejudices against them (voluntary surrender of power and fixed seasonal cycle being things they have trouble grasping).</div> </div> </div> </div>This is a great idea. The Social Maneuvering system is a robust framework that can be adapted to various situations. I based Forsaken 2nd ed's tracking system on it and beat it into a new shape. <br /> <br /> Defeating the True Fae through social 'combat' is thematically appropriate and something the Others should be worried about. I hope to see more based on it in future releases.<br /> <br /> I have a few ideas how Oneiromancy (and Oneiromachy) could be revised based on the Social Maneuvering system - I don't recall from the outline how those areas are being changed for 2nd ed, if at all.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-25T19:47:42-08:00","id":350312,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bunyip</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/341562-preliminary-outline-for-changeling-the-lost-second-edition?p=349734#post349734\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This is a great idea. The Social Maneuvering system is a robust framework that can be adapted to various situations. I based Forsaken 2nd ed's tracking system on it and beat it into a new shape.<br /> <br /> Defeating the True Fae through social 'combat' is thematically appropriate and something the Others should be worried about. I hope to see more based on it in future releases.<br /> <br /> I have a few ideas how Oneiromancy (and Oneiromachy) could be revised based on the Social Maneuvering system - I don't recall from the outline how those areas are being changed for 2nd ed, if at all.</div> </div> </div> </div>My one issue with the Social Maneuvering system, as presented in GMC, is that it presumes this long, gradual, process where you can spend weeks trying to convince someone. My games never seem to work out that way. The PCs are generally pressed for time and have, at best, hours to convince someone and I'm not really sure what to do with it then.<br /> <br /> So, just, if you use it to let characters engage with the True Fae or the Huntsmen in some sort of Story Combat, it would be nice to give some context as to what the expected scenario will look like and what to do if you want to compress it down or make it longer. Like, if the default is that you spend, say, a session evading the Fae while figuring out more about it and ultimately end up getting it to say it's name backwards (or whatever), I'd like some advice on what to do if you want to resolve that event in a single scene or if I wan to stretch it out for a multi-session adventure, either as a subplot or the main plot.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":226,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","user":"BrilliantRain","date":". 12-25-2014, 10:53 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-25T21:30:50-08:00","id":350384,"title":"","content":"Agreed that different tasks require different time frames. That's why I referred to Social Maneuvering as a framework to be adapted. Forsaken's tracking can be resolved in a single roll, or a contested series, all with clear time frame guidelines. I would expect outwitting True Fae via Social Maneuvering would have specified times based on what you're trying to accomplish, and how to compress some of those activities to a single roll or scene (like tracking).<br /> <br /> Similarly, if dream manipulation used the social system for inspiration, I'd guess that the guidelines would be for how to accomplish everything within (at most) a few hours (objective), and how this time could be subjectively very different, because dreams. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-25T21:53:19-08:00","id":350397,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BrilliantRain</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/341562-preliminary-outline-for-changeling-the-lost-second-edition?p=350312#post350312\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> My one issue with the Social Maneuvering system, as presented in GMC, is that it presumes this long, gradual, process where you can spend weeks trying to convince someone. My games never seem to work out that way. The PCs are generally pressed for time and have, at best, hours to convince someone and I'm not really sure what to do with it then.</div> </div> </div> </div>In my experience, if the players don't have a long time to accomplish something, they a) manipulate the impressions so the action can be completed quickly, which tends to lead to more interesting drama, or b) find a different solution. But most of the time, it comes down to manipulating impressions.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-25T23:33:41-08:00","id":350476,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MachineIV</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/341562-preliminary-outline-for-changeling-the-lost-second-edition?p=350397#post350397\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In my experience, if the players don't have a long time to accomplish something, they a) manipulate the impressions so the action can be completed quickly, which tends to lead to more interesting drama, or b) find a different solution. But most of the time, it comes down to manipulating impressions.</div> </div> </div> </div>So why Social Maneuvering system takes this so long to accomplish? I understand that some favors would need those weeks to be pressed, but most <b>should</b> take a few days of preparation at most - 1,2 events, in time of 3-4 evenings should make a case most of the time. But from my reading of rules it looks like you need to spend at least half of month to convince people you <b>know</b> better ( Allies, Contacts etc. ) for something bigger. And most actions will need weeks to complete. A bit overstatement here, in POV.<br /> <br /> As to outsmarting the Fae with new subsystem - I would think it should be some actions you do in time frame of hours for &quot;casual&quot; banishment to Faerie - it really should be a thing to go one one session alone. But the total destruction of Keeper would be a more one of major chronicle plot lines - so here, I would aim for weeks more.<br /> <br /> And no months - in most games &quot;main plot&quot; is only one plot to solve by motley. If you have multiple Keepers for you PCs killing each one should not take more like 4-5 weeks. Players still will need to split that time for deciding <b>who's</b> Keeper to destroy, how to balance politics in region and if they want to sped time to get back in their mortal and family life. All in all, aiming for chronicle to take about half year of time is reasonable time frame for moderate game, I think.<br /> <br /> Note: I'm known for making more intense games with shorter time frames - like 1 season of our <b>Mage</b> game took a 3 months of in-game time. Or my &quot;newbie&quot; intridcutionray game of <b>Werewolf</b> took 1 month only. But still I think that &quot;typical&quot; game in nWoD setting should take about half year of in-game time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 12-26-2014, 02:37 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-25T23:43:08-08:00","id":350502,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/341562-preliminary-outline-for-changeling-the-lost-second-edition?p=350476#post350476\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So why Social Maneuvering system takes this so long to accomplish? I understand that some favors would need those weeks to be pressed, but most <b>should</b> take a few days of preparation at most - 1,2 events, in time of 3-4 evenings should make a case most of the time. But from my reading of rules it looks like you need to spend at least half of month to convince people you <b>know</b> better ( Allies, Contacts etc. ) for something bigger. And most actions will need weeks to complete. A bit overstatement here, in POV.</div> </div> </div> </div>I suspect it is to prevent things like <a href=\"http://www.giantitp.com/comics/oots0767.html\" target=\"_blank\">this</a>, where a diplomatic situation ends up being boiled down to single roll that can do ridiculous things if you are higher level (yes I know the comic is dealing with bluff and things that are mostly not diplomatic, but it covers the spirit nicely). Personally, I like the longer time that it takes to convince people of things. If its a trivial matter, the Storyteller can always reduce the number of doors required. The slower pace more realistically simulates trying to cultivate a relationship to get what you want.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-26T00:23:54-08:00","id":350510,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Second Chances</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/341562-preliminary-outline-for-changeling-the-lost-second-edition?p=350502#post350502\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I suspect it is to prevent things like <a href=\"http://www.giantitp.com/comics/oots0767.html\" target=\"_blank\">this</a>, where a diplomatic situation ends up being boiled down to single roll that can do ridiculous things if you are higher level (yes I know the comic is dealing with bluff and things that are mostly not diplomatic, but it covers the spirit nicely). Personally, I like the longer time that it takes to convince people of things. If its a trivial matter, the Storyteller can always reduce the number of doors required. The slower pace more realistically simulates trying to cultivate a relationship to get what you want.</div> </div> </div> </div>I get this, but all the games I runed or played were based on taking actions <b>now</b>. When using best diplomacy mechanism that takes weeks to use confront with violence - you will almost always get violence, as players <b>and</b> PCs want to solve matter quickest. Construction of Social Maneuvering makes it unusable in real play, a bit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-26T01:16:43-08:00","id":350521,"title":"","content":"That's somewhat like saying that just because my last game didn't have any full combat scenes, the combat mechanics were constructed in an unusable fashion.<br /> <br /> It's easily usable in play in two basic ways that don't involve weeks of in-universe time:<br /> <br /> 1) Building a solid &quot;face&quot; PC that's built to annihilate Doors. High Socials, Sympathetic, Fast-talk, appropriate Professional Training... and remembering that most characters are not going to have a lot of Doors (base is <b>lower</b> of Resolve and Composure). I can easily make a character (though a bit above starting level to be completely unstoppable in this regard) that will smack 4 Doors down on the first roll. That means for an average person, I can ask them to work against their Virtue and an Aspiration, and still convince them it's a good idea. Getting a Good Impression doesn't even take a roll, and basically just takes a decent approach. So that's down to 1 day. A scene to get to know the target, and preferably suss out their Vice? Easy Excellent Impression and we're down to an hour to bust through most people, and possibly Perfect where it just takes a turn. Using the &quot;best diplomacy mechanism&quot; only takes weeks if your character isn't built for it; just like pretty much anything else.<br /> <br /> 2) Don't want to deal with that? Force some doors. Forcing doors ignores the Impression section completely. It's fast and brutal. It is, easily, in the same time frame as combat.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-26T02:54:55-08:00","id":350546,"title":"","content":"Thanks <b>Heavy Arms</b> for remembering those little details about Social Maneuvering. Now waiting for devs say on &quot;Fae Combat&quot; lenghts. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 12-26-2014, 12:40 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-26T06:52:04-08:00","id":350632,"title":"","content":"I don't think Social Maneuvering is unusuable in play, in more realistic framework you probably cannot convince important people and institutions into doing what you want without serious preparations and negotiations taking time. Talking here about the mortal world.<br /> <br /> For True Fae, don't extend that system, a new one taking into account they are beings with alien mindset should be implemented.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cI am absolute, I am perfect, I am supreme. I shall be eternal. My tragedy, is that there is no other fate for me. My powerlessness was that I couldn\u2019t subjugate my journey to the gods, while dreaming of rebirth at the end of distant time, like other pharaohs.\u201d Ramesses II, Fate/Prototype: Argent Fragments.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2918-kat","name":"Kat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2918_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1762"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-26T09:42:38-08:00","id":350706,"title":"","content":"As reading <b>Equinox Road</b> I would advice &quot;Fae Combat&quot; system lenghts as those:<br /> <br /> &quot;Banishing&quot; Actor Fae to Arcadia - matter of hours<br /> Destroying one of Titles ( Actor, Whisps, Prop, Realm ) - matter of weeks<br /> Destroying fully True Fae - matter of months","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 12-26-2014, 04:08 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-26T11:40:29-08:00","id":350810,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/341562-preliminary-outline-for-changeling-the-lost-second-edition?p=350706#post350706\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Banishing Actor Fae to Arcadia - matter of hours<br /> Destroying one of Titles ( Actor, Whisps, Prop, Realm ) - matter of weeks<br /> Destroying fully True Fae - matter of months</div> </div> </div> </div>Three thoughts on that:<br /> <br /> 1) I doubt that any rules would be so specific with times frames like those to apply to every True Fae - the beings are too mutable and fickle to all be defined in hours/weeks/months;<br /> <br /> 2) If talking about Changelings, your suggested times seem entirely too fast. If a True Fae actually comes to town, banishing it should be a triumph and not an afternoon's work. Destroying a Title (if Changelings even know such things exist) would be a major undertaking and be the focus of a chapter in a chronicle. And actually destroying a True Fae would be the climax of an entire chronicle, which could be any length of time, from months to years, to generations.<br /> <br /> 3) If talking about True Fae vs True Fae, specific times are irrelevant. Arcadian battles could burn out in the supernova of seconds, or last centuries in a great war that expands and consumes surrounding countries as the two Queens fight. The time taken has no relationship to real world passage of time, as time is as mutable in Arcadia as every other negotiable aspect of reality.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-26T12:28:37-08:00","id":350848,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bunyip</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/341562-preliminary-outline-for-changeling-the-lost-second-edition?p=350810#post350810\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1) I doubt that any rules would be so specific with times frames like those to apply to every True Fae - the beings are too mutable and fickle to all be defined in hours/weeks/months;</div> </div> </div> </div>But do not Social Maneuvering is based on actions that have a defined length? Like bribing once a week, or something? If you use the framework, you do not define actions like this?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bunyip</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/341562-preliminary-outline-for-changeling-the-lost-second-edition?p=350810#post350810\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">2) If talking about Changelings, your suggested times seem entirely too fast. If a True Fae actually comes to town, banishing it should be a triumph and not an afternoon's work. Destroying a Title (if Changelings even know such things exist) would be a major undertaking and be the focus of a chapter in a chronicle. And actually destroying a True Fae would be the climax of an entire chronicle, which could be any length of time, from months to years, to generations.</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe it's written material, but in play, I really do not see this. For one, most games maybe goes two-three years for <b>very</b> long played games. From last 15 years of playing WW games I do not remember any nWoD ( or even cWoD ) game I heard would last longer, in-game, time than that. To run generation you need to run like a game sessions for like 3 generations real time. So at most games should aim to years duration, at most. Taking in consideration for classical chronicle is about 3-5 PCs, I really think real destroying one Keeper should be at year action at most - because they will be other plots in games, and at least 3 times &quot;resolve a thing with a Keeper&quot;. And maybe I'm wrong, but are not solving relation with your Fetch and Keeper a bit central part of <b>Changeling</b> chronicle?<br /> <br /> For two, banishing should be able to be done in matter of hours - because in longer run it would be unnecessary. If I remember correctly <b>Autumn Nightmares</b>, Actors are destroyed on Earth after hours of Wyrd they have. So yeah, it should be an afternoon's work - if you know what you are doing. Because later it would not be useful to do - Fae Actor will be &quot;killed&quot; or become Charlatan ( if Lost even new they can lived this ).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bunyip</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/341562-preliminary-outline-for-changeling-the-lost-second-edition?p=350810#post350810\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">3) If talking about True Fae vs True Fae, specific times are irrelevant. Arcadian battles could burn out in the supernova of seconds, or last centuries in a great war that expands and consumes surrounding countries as the two Queens fight. The time taken has no relationship to real world passage of time, as time is as mutable in Arcadia as every other negotiable aspect of reality.</div> </div> </div> </div>Get this and affirm. But we are talking here about &quot;Fae Combat&quot; for changeling on Earth based on Social Maneuvering, are we not?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 12-26-2014, 03:32 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-26T12:35:17-08:00","id":350853,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Maybe it's wirten material, but in play, I really do not see this. For one, most games maybe goes two-three years for very long played games. I do not remeber any nWoD ( or even cWoD ) game I heard would last longer, in-game, time than that. To run generation you need to run like a game sessions for like 3 generations real time. So at most games should aim to years duration, at most. Taking in considration for classical game is about 3-5 PCs, I really think real destroying once Keeper should be at year at most - becuase they will be other plots in games, and at least 3 times &quot;resolve a thing with a Keeper&quot;. </div> </div> </div>Timeskips are your friends.<br /> <br /> Realtalk, Social Maneuvering system is not apt to represent the reality of True Fae even with modified rules. It's better to create a new system from scratch, or leave it to narrative and Storyteller's fiat.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cI am absolute, I am perfect, I am supreme. I shall be eternal. My tragedy, is that there is no other fate for me. My powerlessness was that I couldn\u2019t subjugate my journey to the gods, while dreaming of rebirth at the end of distant time, like other pharaohs.\u201d Ramesses II, Fate/Prototype: Argent Fragments.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2918-kat","name":"Kat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2918_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1762"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-26T13:01:19-08:00","id":350863,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/341562-preliminary-outline-for-changeling-the-lost-second-edition?p=350848#post350848\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But do not Social Maneuvering is based on actions that have a defined length?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think you missed that we're talking about expanding and adapting the social framework, not using the system exactly 'as is', with its presently defined time frames. The concepts within the system are more important (IMO) than its current parameters.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-26T16:07:06-08:00","id":351000,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/341562-preliminary-outline-for-changeling-the-lost-second-edition?p=350476#post350476\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So why Social Maneuvering system takes this so long to accomplish? I understand that some favors would need those weeks to be pressed, but most <b>should</b> take a few days of preparation at most - 1,2 events, in time of 3-4 evenings should make a case most of the time. But from my reading of rules it looks like you need to spend at least half of month to convince people you <b>know</b> better ( Allies, Contacts etc. ) for something bigger. And most actions will need weeks to complete. A bit overstatement here, in POV.</div> </div> </div> </div>I have never once had someone try to maneuver someone with the worst possible impressions. Every single time, without fail, the players will either try to improve impressions (which isn't actually that difficult, and adds to the story), or force the Doors. I also don't make people maneuver for their social Merits, since there are already defined rules for how those are used. <br /> <br /> I'm sorry you've had these experiences. But I've literally used these rules hundreds of times, and never once had those experiences.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-26T21:13:49-08:00","id":351293,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bunyip</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/341562-preliminary-outline-for-changeling-the-lost-second-edition?p=349734#post349734\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is a great idea. The Social Maneuvering system is a robust framework that can be adapted to various situations. I based Forsaken 2nd ed's tracking system on it and beat it into a new shape.</div> </div> </div> </div>Now THAT'S a juicy tidbit!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Cxuog44JenzbN7GaAyRqDO4DXce9VGv6ybaCv9yYsPk/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Simulacre: An Alternative Morality Stat for Prometheans</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/9523-the-alchemy-lab-homebrew-athanors\" target=\"_blank\">Homebrew Athanors</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/887-metamurpho","name":"Metamurpho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar887_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"228"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-27T21:45:52-08:00","id":352325,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/341562-preliminary-outline-for-changeling-the-lost-second-edition?p=350848#post350848\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Maybe it's written material, but in play, I really do not see this. For one, most games maybe goes two-three years for <b>very</b> long played games. From last 15 years of playing WW games I do not remember any nWoD ( or even cWoD ) game I heard would last longer, in-game, time than that.</div> </div> </div> </div>I ran a Mage: Ascension campaign that spanned over forty years (1842-1888) in game time and about three years in real time. We would have fairly regular jumps of six months to several years in between plots. This allows the characters to go from low level members of the Order of Reason to some of its most powerful members in London (fighting against the evolution into the Technocracy, consequently). It also let them interact with their children and grandchildren. It was awesome. I highly recommend it.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Eric Christian Berg</b><br /> <i>Onyx Path Freelancer</i><br /> Promethean: The Created Second Edition, Dark Eras Companion","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2019-eberg","name":"eberg","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2019_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"284"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-28T00:34:31-08:00","id":352428,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>eberg</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/341562-preliminary-outline-for-changeling-the-lost-second-edition?p=352325#post352325\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I ran a Mage: Ascension campaign that spanned over forty years (1842-1888) in game time and about three years in real time. We would have fairly regular jumps of six months to several years in between plots. This allows the characters to go from low level members of the Order of Reason to some of its most powerful members in London (fighting against the evolution into the Technocracy, consequently). It also let them interact with their children and grandchildren. It was awesome. I highly recommend it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you, I maybe use this idea for my planed game about creation of Free Council in XIX <b>Awakening</b> setting. But still - it's more a exception than the rule really. Most games I seen or heard of are still made in most of year, maybe two of game time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-28T05:58:17-08:00","id":352582,"title":"","content":"One of games I recall has not even finished Day 1 yet during last three years. It's when you flesh out every NPC with precision beyond realm of Gods,","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cI am absolute, I am perfect, I am supreme. I shall be eternal. My tragedy, is that there is no other fate for me. My powerlessness was that I couldn\u2019t subjugate my journey to the gods, while dreaming of rebirth at the end of distant time, like other pharaohs.\u201d Ramesses II, Fate/Prototype: Argent Fragments.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2918-kat","name":"Kat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2918_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1762"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-29T08:21:40-08:00","id":353759,"title":"","content":"One question I am curious about, will there be more support for playing characters truly 'lost out of time' this time? One of the things about the last edition I hated was how it was basically stated categorically that Lost never really came back after more than 50 or so years, and even with the merit/flaw 100 years was the limit. I like stories of being 'out of time' as it were, so not having that annoying line in the corebook saying that would be wonderful. Because like it or not, a lot of GMs will enforce that rule, limiting my char options should I want to make one.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/448-dulahan","name":"Dulahan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar448_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"115"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-29T11:02:33-08:00","id":353879,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dulahan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/341562-preliminary-outline-for-changeling-the-lost-second-edition?p=353759#post353759\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One question I am curious about, will there be more support for playing characters truly 'lost out of time' this time? One of the things about the last edition I hated was how it was basically stated categorically that Lost never really came back after more than 50 or so years, and even with the merit/flaw 100 years was the limit. I like stories of being 'out of time' as it were, so not having that annoying line in the corebook saying that would be wonderful. Because like it or not, a lot of GMs will enforce that rule, limiting my char options should I want to make one.</div> </div> </div> </div>How would you make fetches relevant to your character in that case?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I call the Integrity-analogue the &quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/822559-trying-to-understand-the-morality-system?p=825008#post825008\" target=\"_blank\">subjective stat</a>&quot;.<br /> An explanation how to <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/913221-using-social-manuevering\" target=\"_blank\">use Social Manuevering</a>.<br /> Guanxi Explanations: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=787824#post787824\" target=\"_blank\">1</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=788173#post788173\" target=\"_blank\">2</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/833863-mages-and-trading-favors?p=834531#post834531\" target=\"_blank\">3</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2758-errol216","name":"Errol216","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-29T11:05:48-08:00","id":353893,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Errol216</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/341562-preliminary-outline-for-changeling-the-lost-second-edition?p=353879#post353879\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How would you make fetches relevant to your character in that case?</div> </div> </div> </div>Or\u2026 <i>anything</i>, really, given the entire basis by which the Lost get back to Earth on their own?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-29T11:19:51-08:00","id":353904,"title":"","content":"Winter Soldier* showcases a good summary of the problem with making the time gap too large. Yes, Steve is certainly Lost, but he's so lost that he has to forge new anchors in the world-he has nothing of his life to build his roads with. Lost characters, by contrast, are lost enough that getting home isn't easy, but they can still build their roads out of their ruined lives.<br /> <br /> *I am not saying that Winter Soldier is a bad movie, for the record, it's quite good, but it highlights the problems of the concept for the basic Lost chronicle.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-30T12:59:17-08:00","id":355045,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Errol216</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/341562-preliminary-outline-for-changeling-the-lost-second-edition?p=353879#post353879\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How would you make fetches relevant to your character in that case?</div> </div> </div> </div>Since when did every character have a Fetch to begin with? It wasn't a requirement. It even says flat out in the book they aren't an 'every time' thing. Just a potential complication.<br /> <br /> Being that lost in time is AT LEAST as interesting a story and a problem with identity as dealing with a fetch is. And in certain contexts, probably more so. Especially in more social and long term based, large scale games like LARP and Mu*s.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/448-dulahan","name":"Dulahan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar448_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"115"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-30T20:02:27-08:00","id":355353,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dulahan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/341562-preliminary-outline-for-changeling-the-lost-second-edition?p=355045#post355045\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Since when did every character have a Fetch to begin with? It wasn't a requirement. It even says flat out in the book they aren't an 'every time' thing. Just a potential complication.<br /> <br /> Being that lost in time is AT LEAST as interesting a story and a problem with identity as dealing with a fetch is. And in certain contexts, probably more so. Especially in more social and long term based, large scale games like LARP and Mu*s.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't often do this, but I'm going to take you to task for ignoring the question I added as a rider to Errol's, because it's a pretty fucking important one.<br /> <br /> Changelings find their way back to the world from Faerie by the correspondence of their memories with things that are still around in a recognizable form. &quot;Fish out of temporal water&quot; stories of the complete-future-shock variety implied by an outer limit of a century (when the last century has arguably had the most rapid changes in the state of civilization and the world) don't work with that outside the context of &quot;the Fae dumped a loyalist on Earth for their amusement.&quot;<br /> <br /> There are other games better equipped for that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":111,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","user":"Satchel","date":". 12-30-2014, 11:06 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-31T01:56:01-08:00","id":355540,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dulahan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/341562-preliminary-outline-for-changeling-the-lost-second-edition?p=355045#post355045\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Especially in more social and long term based, large scale games like LARP and Mu*s.</div> </div> </div> </div>I had a longer response, but since you're being so defensive about it, I'm just going to say this: the second edition isn't, as far as I'm aware, expanding the focus from tabletops to LARPs and MU*s. If you want to do that, you shouldn't be asking the designers to do it; it's just not possible for them to do a good job of it, since none of their playtesting will cover that area. Recognize that such an expansion <i>should</i> come with extensive effort on your own part to revise the rules to suit a different setting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I call the Integrity-analogue the &quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/822559-trying-to-understand-the-morality-system?p=825008#post825008\" target=\"_blank\">subjective stat</a>&quot;.<br /> An explanation how to <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/913221-using-social-manuevering\" target=\"_blank\">use Social Manuevering</a>.<br /> Guanxi Explanations: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=787824#post787824\" target=\"_blank\">1</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=788173#post788173\" target=\"_blank\">2</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/833863-mages-and-trading-favors?p=834531#post834531\" target=\"_blank\">3</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2758-errol216","name":"Errol216","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-31T07:02:30-08:00","id":355732,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/341562-preliminary-outline-for-changeling-the-lost-second-edition?p=355353#post355353\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Changelings find their way back to the world from Faerie by the correspondence of their memories with things that are still around in a recognizable form. &quot;Fish out of temporal water&quot; stories of the complete-future-shock variety implied by an outer limit of a century (when the last century has arguably had the most rapid changes in the state of civilization and the world) don't work with that outside the context of &quot;the Fae dumped a loyalist on Earth for their amusement.&quot;<br /> <br /> There are other games better equipped for that.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I image that &quot;out of time&quot; changelings would pop out around national landmarks, historical buildings, and things that wouldn't have changed too much. You'd also probably find more of them in Europe and Asia, as they have a bit longer of history of building permanent structures.<br /> <br /> Also, with Glamour being so attached to emotion, they could be brought back by upsurges of of emotion similar to ones that defined their lives when they were taken. A Scrooge finds himself on wall street, or an African Slave emerging in the midst of racially charged protests.<br /> <br /> I think the idea of trying to forge a new life out of nothing is at least as interesting as trying to reclaim the life that was taken from you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2283,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2283-andreamus","user":"andreamus","date":".  typos.. 12-31-2014, 01:01 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2283-andreamus","name":"andreamus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2283_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"95"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-31T11:24:51-08:00","id":355889,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>andreamus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/341562-preliminary-outline-for-changeling-the-lost-second-edition?p=355732#post355732\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I image that &quot;out of time&quot; changelings would pop out around national landmarks, historical buildings, and things that wouldn't have changed too much.</div> </div> </div> </div>With the exception of the last (which is too broad to say anything about), all of these can have &quot;the Fae have never replicated a discrete pop-culture image&quot; pointed to as a rationale for why the Lost don't utterly ventilate the notion of fae being secretive by having anachronistic refugees pop out at high-profile locations regularly enough to justify negating the guideline.<br /> <br /> Even without that aspect, with Arcadian time being fluid, why would the wayward turn up in an era significantly later than their relevance to the world? The matter of a fetch may be a non-universal one, but it doesn't change the fact that memory-of-the-world-as-navigational-tool is something of a two-way street \u2014 &quot;aren't you the guy who died ten years ago?&quot; is a stronger hold on the changeling than &quot;you look like you stepped out of the Industrial Revolution.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I think the idea of trying to forge a new life out of nothing is at least as interesting as trying to reclaim the life that was taken from you. </div> </div> </div>Understanding that Clarity has some serious things to say about losing significant touchstones of your mortal identity means I rather axiomatically disagree.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":111,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","user":"Satchel","date":".  Missing word and formatting. 12-31-2014, 02:27 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-31T11:37:33-08:00","id":355912,"title":"","content":"My $0.02:<br /> <br /> Out-of-time changelings (say, within the last hundred years or so) are possible, though rare. They generally need a very *strong* tie to the Mortal world in order to find their way back, and the tie needs to be something which won't have changed dramatically since their abduction: The ancestral family home, the office (maintained by a historical society) in which they performed the work which consumed their life, or the traditional barracks of the armed force in which they served their country could all serve as beacons for the return trip. Again, however, such recoveries are *much* more rare than those which occur within a natural human lifespan - say, 50 years or so to represent adulthood. <br /> <br /> This allows for the fish out of temporal water storylines while also not watering down the thematics of the venue too much. As for Clarity, well, a newly arrived Changeling is always going to have Clarity troubles until their grasp on reality firms up again. I'd say these guys just have a bit more trouble than most.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1168-hobbitguy1420","name":"HobbitGuy1420","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"332"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-01T13:47:34-08:00","id":356857,"title":"","content":"It's too bad that the Outliine is gone. It kind of makes newcomers nervous coming into the topic.<br /> <br /> As for me, when I saw that it would be called The Huntsmen Chronicle, my mind immediately went to The Wyld Hunt. And given from what I read from the posts, it seems highly likely that this may be the case.<br /> <br /> From what I read (fantasy novels), The Wyld Hunt:<br /> <br /> 1. Can't be controlled by the Fae, unless there are favors to be given (meaning that they are not with the Gentry).<br /> <br /> 2. They leave an hour before Dawn.<br /> <br /> In essence, the Huntsmen are the Boba Fetts of Lost.<br /> <br /> It's interesting that players can now create their own Courts. That gives high hopes that the Twilight Court will upgrade from an Entitlement. The only pause is that we must expect that players will severely abuse the creation rules for Courts as with Entitlements, in hopes of seeing their homebrewed Court become official by Onyx Path. Kind of like what we saw for Mage Legacies.<br /> <br /> Playing a character that's either Seemingless and/or Kithless will be tricky, given the subtle nuances of the creation process. Plus, how would you play one of those?<br /> <br /> I hope that the blog starts up soon so I can catch up.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/891-jackalopevegas","name":"JackalopeVegas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"246"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-01T15:40:01-08:00","id":356974,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JackalopeVegas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/341562-preliminary-outline-for-changeling-the-lost-second-edition?p=356857#post356857\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As for me, when I saw that it would be called The Huntsmen Chronicle, my mind immediately went to The Wyld Hunt. And given from what I read from the posts, it seems highly likely that this may be the case.<br /> <br /> From what I read (fantasy novels), The Wyld Hunt:<br /> <br /> 1. Can't be controlled by the Fae, unless there are favors to be given (meaning that they are not with the Gentry).<br /> <br /> 2. They leave an hour before Dawn.</div> </div> </div> </div>I do not get a concept of Wyld Hunt, even if in our Polish, Slavic myths it comes from time to time. But I get it's more anglo-saxon thing. Could someone describe me a basics of those Wyld Hunt myths, so I could understand a difference between been snatch by True Fae and a Huntsman?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JackalopeVegas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/341562-preliminary-outline-for-changeling-the-lost-second-edition?p=356857#post356857\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Playing a character that's either Seemingless and/or Kithless will be tricky, given the subtle nuances of the creation process. Plus, how would you play one of those?</div> </div> </div> </div>Been described before - Seemingless are those of changelings still in Arcadia, obvious Loyalists or that returned with some weird happenstance. Coming to freehold of this Lost would rise questions about here loyalty with True Fae, and yes, it will be much harder play. But I would play one, even for challenge. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Kithless are those that were free roaming in Faerie and returned on Earth. You are just more &quot;hobgoblin-like&quot;, than proper Fae. It's much more simpler than you think about it. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 01-01-2015, 06:44 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-01T16:13:26-08:00","id":357019,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> But I get it's more anglo-saxon thing. </div> </div> </div>Celtic and Germanic. <br /> <br /> And wiki is your friend: <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wild_Hunt\" target=\"_blank\">http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wild_Hunt</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cI am absolute, I am perfect, I am supreme. I shall be eternal. My tragedy, is that there is no other fate for me. My powerlessness was that I couldn\u2019t subjugate my journey to the gods, while dreaming of rebirth at the end of distant time, like other pharaohs.\u201d Ramesses II, Fate/Prototype: Argent Fragments.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2918-kat","name":"Kat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2918_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1762"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-01T17:02:56-08:00","id":357068,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JackalopeVegas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/341562-preliminary-outline-for-changeling-the-lost-second-edition?p=356857#post356857\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As for me, when I saw that it would be called The Huntsmen Chronicle, my mind immediately went to The Wyld Hunt. And given from what I read from the posts, it seems highly likely that this may be the case.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Huntsman_(Snow_White)\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/7/78/Snow_White_and_the_Seven_Dwarfs_2.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=index&amp;utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Huntsman_(Snow_White)\" target=\"_blank\"> Snow White - Wikipedia </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Huntsman_(Snow_White)\" target=\"_blank\"> http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Huntsman_(Snow_White) </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I call the Integrity-analogue the &quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/822559-trying-to-understand-the-morality-system?p=825008#post825008\" target=\"_blank\">subjective stat</a>&quot;.<br /> An explanation how to <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/913221-using-social-manuevering\" target=\"_blank\">use Social Manuevering</a>.<br /> Guanxi Explanations: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=787824#post787824\" target=\"_blank\">1</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=788173#post788173\" target=\"_blank\">2</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/833863-mages-and-trading-favors?p=834531#post834531\" target=\"_blank\">3</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2758-errol216","name":"Errol216","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-01T17:10:51-08:00","id":357074,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kat</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/341562-preliminary-outline-for-changeling-the-lost-second-edition?p=357019#post357019\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Celtic and Germanic.<br /> <br /> And wiki is your friend: <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wild_Hunt\" target=\"_blank\">http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wild_Hunt</a></div> </div> </div> </div>Still, not seeing how idea states clearly about division by True Fae and Huntsman, here. All I see &quot;there are some mythological beings that will steal you, if you come across they journey on the sky&quot;. I do not know of any concrete story of Polish origin using this theme, but I know there is new <i>Witcher</i> game named Wild Hunt on this premise ( <i>Dziki Gon</i> in Polish ). <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Still, I assume that &quot;everybody looking for adult Ciri&quot; is not a core or this interesting for <b>Changeling </b>part of the myth? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-05T05:10:42-08:00","id":360123,"title":"","content":"Have to agree with Wyrdhamster, I always considered the stories about the Wild Hunt as the classic example of True Fae. Sure, in some versions the hunters get released when the Hunt returns home more or less unchanged, but is that much more than a distortion from escapees or Loyalists?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4560-madfox11","name":"Madfox11","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"172"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-05T07:01:54-08:00","id":360188,"title":"","content":"Unshackle your mind, broaden your horizons.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-05T10:12:17-08:00","id":360275,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Errol216</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/341562-preliminary-outline-for-changeling-the-lost-second-edition?p=355540#post355540\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I had a longer response, but since you're being so defensive about it, I'm just going to say this: the second edition isn't, as far as I'm aware, expanding the focus from tabletops to LARPs and MU*s. If you want to do that, you shouldn't be asking the designers to do it; it's just not possible for them to do a good job of it, since none of their playtesting will cover that area. Recognize that such an expansion <i>should</i> come with extensive effort on your own part to revise the rules to suit a different setting.</div> </div> </div> </div>I didn't think I was being defensive at all, just responding to the implication every changeling needed a Fetch, which seemed pretty defensive and 'one true wayist' on its own, so I countered with how it isn't the only thing that happens.<br /> <br /> And mentioning long term play options, which usually do just use the core system without changes. *shrugs*<br /> <br /> I mean, I really don't have an issue with lengthy times away being rare. I just think they're a type of story that is at least as interesting as dealing with a fetch. It's a different sort of challenge for the lost, but able to be something very interesting all the same.<br /> <br /> And belatedly to Satchel, I thought I did respond, sorry you didn't see it as such.<br /> <br /> Finally I add this, remember, not all Lost 'escape' on their own either. sometimes the Gentry let them go, which is still another set of messed up problems.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/448-dulahan","name":"Dulahan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar448_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"115"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-05T10:48:29-08:00","id":360296,"title":"","content":"Piggybacking on what the last poster said, I've heard that Kith and Seeming are based on how you escaped Arcadia rather than what happened to you. Does that mean those let go rather than escaping would lack both?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-05T11:04:09-08:00","id":360299,"title":"","content":"Kith represents your Durance. What you went through in Arcadia, what role your Keeper gave you, and what form your time there shaped you as. Seeming represents your escape. How you took back your agency and how you survived the journey back.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","name":"YeOfLittleFaith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar188_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-05T12:20:50-08:00","id":360413,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>YeOfLittleFaith</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/341562-preliminary-outline-for-changeling-the-lost-second-edition?p=360299#post360299\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Kith represents your Durance. What you went through in Arcadia, what role your Keeper gave you, and what form your time there shaped you as. Seeming represents your escape. How you took back your agency and how you survived the journey back.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you for answering!So I'm assuming that Kith and Seeming are decidedly decoupled compared to First Edition?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-05T12:28:44-08:00","id":360423,"title":"","content":"From what was in the outline, yeah, seems so.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","name":"YeOfLittleFaith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar188_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-05T13:25:17-08:00","id":360518,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ZealousChristian24</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/341562-preliminary-outline-for-changeling-the-lost-second-edition?p=360296#post360296\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Piggybacking on what the last poster said, I've heard that Kith and Seeming are based on how you escaped Arcadia rather than what happened to you. Does that mean those let go rather than escaping would lack both?</div> </div> </div> </div>You'd find this of interest:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/232331-changeling-2-0-brainspew-1-kiths-seemings\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/filedata/fetch?filedataid=1074\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/232331-changeling-2-0-brainspew-1-kiths-seemings\"> Changeling 2.0 Brainspew 1: Kiths/Seemings - Onyx Path Forums </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/232331-changeling-2-0-brainspew-1-kiths-seemings\"> http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/232331-changeling-2-0-brainspew-1-kiths-seemings </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> I'll start off this experiment with a brainspew, to show you where we're thinking. We're sort of reversing the roles of Kiths and Seemings. When making a </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I call the Integrity-analogue the &quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/822559-trying-to-understand-the-morality-system?p=825008#post825008\" target=\"_blank\">subjective stat</a>&quot;.<br /> An explanation how to <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/913221-using-social-manuevering\" target=\"_blank\">use Social Manuevering</a>.<br /> Guanxi Explanations: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=787824#post787824\" target=\"_blank\">1</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=788173#post788173\" target=\"_blank\">2</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/833863-mages-and-trading-favors?p=834531#post834531\" target=\"_blank\">3</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2758-errol216","name":"Errol216","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-05T13:36:38-08:00","id":360531,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Errol216</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/341562-preliminary-outline-for-changeling-the-lost-second-edition?p=360518#post360518\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You'd find this of interest:<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/232331-changeling-2-0-brainspew-1-kiths-seemings\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...kiths-seemings</a></div> </div> </div> </div> Oh thank you! This is positively delicious! The only complaint is that I'd prefer that Changelings could learn all Contracts, given time and experience, given their weakness compared to other Supernaturals.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-05T14:38:07-08:00","id":360623,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ZealousChristian24</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/341562-preliminary-outline-for-changeling-the-lost-second-edition?p=360531#post360531\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Oh thank you! This is positively delicious! The only complaint is that I'd prefer that Changelings could learn all Contracts, given time and experience, given their weakness compared to other Supernaturals.</div> </div> </div> </div>Fortunately, you will also find <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/242936-changeling-2-0-brainspew-2-contracts\">this</a> to be of interest. The &quot;Some [Seemings] will be unable to learn other Contracts&quot; line seems to have faded as an idea, as hinted there. From what the Outline depicted, a Universal Contract lists favored Seemings, for which the Contract does an additional or focused thing. If you have a favored Seeming, you buy the Contract and also get that extra benefit for free with your purchase. If you don't, you just get the Contract. Regardless, you can seek out a Changeling with a different Seeming who's willing to teach it, and thereby also learn that Seeming's benefit for 1 experience.<br /> <br /> We'll have to wait and see how Changelings stack up compared to other splats in their 2e forms. There's not been any real mention of it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":558,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","user":"Gaius","date":". 01-05-2015, 05:40 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-05T14:49:55-08:00","id":360629,"title":"","content":"@Gaius: This is going to be FUN, isn't it?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-05T15:04:51-08:00","id":360639,"title":"","content":"I know I've got positive feelings. ^__^ Still kind of mentally changing gears on what 2e Seeming means now (more examples may help), and I'd like to learn more about the Huntsmen, but I'm looking forward to almost every change revealed so far.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-05T18:07:35-08:00","id":360799,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ZealousChristian24</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/341562-preliminary-outline-for-changeling-the-lost-second-edition?p=360531#post360531\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Oh thank you! This is positively delicious! The only complaint is that I'd prefer that Changelings could learn all Contracts, given time and experience, given their weakness compared to other Supernaturals.</div> </div> </div> </div>What weakness compared to other supernaturals?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-05T18:49:45-08:00","id":360821,"title":"","content":"I think there's a general perception that changelings are on the &quot;squishy&quot; side of nWOD supernaturals. They don't have the same default physical endurance that most of the others have, or as ready access to a general healing power (like Mages do). Without a character in the group built to be an effective healer, and the nWOD's general lethality, 1e changelings can be pretty easy to kill.<br /> <br /> I've played enough of CtL that I'm not sure it is 100% accurate, but it certainly can happen with the system. I don't see how Contract pricing really matters to it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-05T19:33:08-08:00","id":360837,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/341562-preliminary-outline-for-changeling-the-lost-second-edition?p=360821#post360821\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think there's a general perception that changelings are on the &quot;squishy&quot; side of nWOD supernaturals. They don't have the same default physical endurance that most of the others have, or as ready access to a general healing power (like Mages do). Without a character in the group built to be an effective healer, and the nWOD's general lethality, 1e changelings can be pretty easy to kill.<br /> <br /> I've played enough of CtL that I'm not sure it is 100% accurate, but it certainly can happen with the system. I don't see how Contract pricing really matters to it.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think in this case, the trick is to not play 1e Changelings with 2e games.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-05T19:39:36-08:00","id":360843,"title":"","content":"In 1e, at least, Contracts were designed to be on the lower level of their dot rating (if I remember right) - this accentuated the Lost's &quot;be careful, stack the deck in your favor, and make sure you have every trick possible in your pocket, because you'll probably need them.&quot; <br /> <br /> Not sure if that thematic is sticking around for 2e - sort of hope it does, 'cuz I like the aesthetic it provides.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1168-hobbitguy1420","name":"HobbitGuy1420","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"332"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-05T19:50:47-08:00","id":360847,"title":"","content":"By the end of my long running Changeling campaign, I had a Wyrd 8 Elemental player stacking Contracts of Elements and Stone (and Dual Kith Gargantuan). &quot;Squishy&quot; quickly stopped being something I associated with Changelings.<br /> <br /> That said, the group's Wizened did tend to go down pretty fast.<br /> <br /> In either case, I don't quite see the link between Contracts and Seemings. That could be partly because the idea that Seemings be related to how you escape has led to my mind almost entirely divorcing them from the physical and metaphysical attributes assigned to them in 1e. An Ogre isn't an &quot;ogre&quot;, just someone who used violence to get away. It might indicate a proclivity towards certain Contracts over others, but that's about it.<br /> <br /> Really, I think what it indicates is that I actually need to read the new Seeming write-ups to figure out what their newly defined meanings actually equate to in the context of the game's universe before I can make any judgement on whether or not the Contract limitations are appropriate.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-05T21:02:21-08:00","id":360910,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Azahul</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/341562-preliminary-outline-for-changeling-the-lost-second-edition?p=360847#post360847\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In either case, I don't quite see the link between Contracts and Seemings. That could be partly because the idea that Seemings be related to how you escape has led to my mind almost entirely divorcing them from the physical and metaphysical attributes assigned to them in 1e. An Ogre isn't an &quot;ogre&quot;, just someone who used violence to get away. It might indicate a proclivity towards certain Contracts over others, but that's about it.<br /> <br /> Really, I think what it indicates is that I actually need to read the new Seeming write-ups to figure out what their newly defined meanings actually equate to in the context of the game's universe before I can make any judgement on whether or not the Contract limitations are appropriate.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm still kinda feeling things out myself, admittedly, and further elaboration and examples would be very welcome. However, I wouldn't presume that an Ogre is &quot;just&quot; someone who used violence to get away. David's made some comments about &quot;the mythology of the Durance,&quot;* and how the Seeming describes an individual regaining agency after having lost it. Kith seems to reflect what the character was made to be in a tale, while Seeming reflects what the character made of herself. If a Changeling in part reflects his Durance's mythology, then surely the action that ended it should leave an impact. It's a powerful act, taking back one's agency; it's not unreasonable the Wyrd might respond in a significant way. Perhaps a sort of, &quot;You've declared that this is what you are, and so this shall you be,&quot; thing.<br /> <br /> * Would adore hearing more about this, by the way. :3 It was likened to how other 2e books are building options into the origin story that reflect character elements, like a Werewolf's pack or a Vampire's Touchstones.**<br /> ** This may be a good time to mention I know basically jack-all about the rest of the World of Darkness. If someone's willing to banish my ignorance about how those character-building options have worked, I'd be obliged.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-05T21:24:03-08:00","id":360920,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gaius</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/341562-preliminary-outline-for-changeling-the-lost-second-edition?p=360910#post360910\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm still kinda feeling things out myself, admittedly, and further elaboration and examples would be very welcome. However, I wouldn't presume that an Ogre is &quot;just&quot; someone who used violence to get away. David's made some comments about &quot;the mythology of the Durance,&quot;* and how the Seeming describes an individual regaining agency after having lost it. Kith seems to reflect what the character was made to be in a tale, while Seeming reflects what the character made of herself. If a Changeling in part reflects his Durance's mythology, then surely the action that ended it should leave an impact. It's a powerful act, taking back one's agency; it's not unreasonable the Wyrd might respond in a significant way. Perhaps a sort of, &quot;You've declared that this is what you are, and so this shall you be,&quot; thing.<br /> <br /> * Would adore hearing more about this, by the way. :3 It was likened to how other 2e books are building options into the origin story that reflect character elements, like a Werewolf's pack or a Vampire's Touchstones.**<br /> ** This may be a good time to mention I know basically jack-all about the rest of the World of Darkness. If someone's willing to banish my ignorance about how those character-building options have worked, I'd be obliged.</div> </div> </div> </div>I guess what I mean is more that Seeming has come to mean something personal, intrinsic to your character, and fundamentally linked to your character's agency, but in doing so doesn't seem to hold much weight anymore in the realm of how that expresses itself in your being a mythological creature (although tying it into the mythology of the Durance, as mentioned, could go a long way towards sorting that out). It's a great concept and I love it, but it leaves me feeling like Seemings aren't all that related to the magical side of being a Changeling, making the decision to limit Contracts by Seeming a little odd. An Ogre used to be an actual fairytale Ogre, to some extent, but a Changeling <i>being</i> an ogre now seems part of their Kith while their Seeming is more indicative of whether or not they actually act like an Ogre.<br /> <br /> That said, the above is purely my initial reaction based on cliff notes, and I'm sure the actual write-ups will lend a great deal more physical weight to the Seeming than my initial reading indicated. Tying &quot;how you gained agency&quot; into &quot;what you look like/the kind of magic you manifest&quot; is naturally a concept that is hard to carry without the full write-ups, I feel.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-05T21:37:23-08:00","id":360929,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MachineIV</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/341562-preliminary-outline-for-changeling-the-lost-second-edition?p=360837#post360837\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think in this case, the trick is to not play 1e Changelings with 2e games.</div> </div> </div> </div>My post was retaining a purely 1e sensibility. The fact that vampires and werewolves seem to be getting a significant &quot;toughness&quot; increase in 2e doesn't help the impression, but we haven't seen what 2e changelings are bringing to the table yet either.<br /> <br /> Even in 1e, all vampires can heal non-agg reflexively and downgrade some sources of damage to bashing, all werewolves have increased healing and access to forums with increased combat stats, all mages had access to shielding spells and anyone could start with enough Life for self healing at a minimum, Prometheans and sin-eaters can revive post death on top of being fairly tough, etc.<br /> <br /> Changelings didn't get any innate boosts to survivability like that, and the main healing powers were locked behind being Spring Court or very limited in the form of goblin fruits. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Azahul</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/341562-preliminary-outline-for-changeling-the-lost-second-edition?p=360847#post360847\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">By the end of my long running Changeling campaign, I had a Wyrd 8 Elemental player stacking Contracts of Elements and Stone (and Dual Kith Gargantuan). &quot;Squishy&quot; quickly stopped being something I associated with Changelings.</div> </div> </div> </div>The issue was never that you couldn't make tough changelings really. The problem was you had to really build a character for it. A combat focused changeling that's been in a campaign long enough to hit Wyrd 8 is nothing to sneeze at. The issue is more than a most of the other splats at power stat 8 have a large number of innate powers/low level powers boosted highly that even non-combat characters would be benefiting from.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-06T05:08:06-08:00","id":361147,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/341562-preliminary-outline-for-changeling-the-lost-second-edition?p=360929#post360929\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Changelings didn't get any innate boosts to survivability like that, and the main healing powers were locked behind being Spring Court or very limited in the form of goblin fruits.</div> </div> </div> </div>Goblin fruit is limited in that access depends entirely up to the GM and in the fact that the game gives no advice at all on how to hand out the fruit in a fun way. If access is easy though, goblin fruit is remarkably cost free healing. It is just a tad too slow to use in combat. Out of combat you can savely assume a Changeling will be fully healed within minutes after gaining access to the right hollow/NPC <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Of course, their biggest strength is in subtility. Keeping them out is very difficult and they have some of the best protections against detection by mortals in the world. At the same time they can invade people's dreams (talk about security risk) or lead others into the Hedge with no hope of escape (Mage excepted perhaps).As a Vampire and a Werewolf I would be very hesitent to anger the local Changeling populace. Sure, killing individuals once found is easy, but I am sure as hell going to get burned indirectly <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Besides, how many people run mixed campaigns? Is the intent of 2e to allow GMs to run such campaigns with ease? Because ultimately, balance between the various supernaturals only matter when different supernaturals sit down at the same table...<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4560-madfox11","name":"Madfox11","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"172"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-06T09:13:25-08:00","id":361374,"title":"","content":"I largely agree.<br /> <br /> However my point was on the perception of changelings in 1e as being &quot;weaker&quot; in direct physical contests thus necessitating having cheap access to a lot of the things you just mentioned.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-08T09:59:09-08:00","id":363618,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MachineIV</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/341562-preliminary-outline-for-changeling-the-lost-second-edition?p=360799#post360799\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> What weakness compared to other supernaturals?</div> </div> </div> </div> Sorry for not seeing this sooner. Basically, as others have said, they are, like Mages, &quot;more human&quot;(that is to say, more squishy) than other Supers, lacking, for example, the basic generic healing power that almost all playable Supers seem to have, as well as the fact Contracts lean towards the lower end of the scale, power-wise. Sorry for derailing the thread; I meant no harm.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-13T22:35:21-08:00","id":369466,"title":"","content":"Personally I'm happy to hear about Tokyo becoming a major changeling setting. There's a lot of Japanese specific folklore that can applied to changeling in interesting ways. I'm looking forward to seeing how they handle getting spirited away and the like. <br /> <br /> Also, Crossing Midnight practically screams Changeling.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2244-nothri","name":"nothri","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"485"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-13T23:50:22-08:00","id":369509,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nothri</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/341562-preliminary-outline-for-changeling-the-lost-second-edition?p=369466#post369466\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Personally I'm happy to hear about Tokyo becoming a major changeling setting. There's a lot of Japanese specific folklore that can applied to changeling in interesting ways. I'm looking forward to seeing how they handle getting spirited away and the like.<br /> <br /> Also, Crossing Midnight practically screams Changeling.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm excited to write it. Truth be told, I haven't given it much thought yet. But, I think it'll be good. I've had a lot of fun doing Tokyo for Vampire, Mage, Werewolf, Beast, and Promethean so far.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-14T19:38:44-08:00","id":370629,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MachineIV</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/341562-preliminary-outline-for-changeling-the-lost-second-edition?p=369509#post369509\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm excited to write it. Truth be told, I haven't given it much thought yet. But, I think it'll be good. I've had a lot of fun doing Tokyo for Vampire, Mage, Werewolf, Beast, and Promethean so far.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I have only had the opportunity to look at Vampire so far but I like what was made of the Tokyo (and other cities) in that setting.<br /> <br /> In case you aren't already familiar with the term, this could relevant to the discussion- <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Spirit_away\" target=\"_blank\">http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Spirit_away</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2244-nothri","name":"nothri","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"485"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-14T19:50:45-08:00","id":370638,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MachineIV</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/341562-preliminary-outline-for-changeling-the-lost-second-edition?p=369509#post369509\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm excited to write it. Truth be told, I haven't given it much thought yet. But, I think it'll be good. I've had a lot of fun doing Tokyo for Vampire, Mage, Werewolf, Beast, and Promethean so far.</div> </div> </div> </div>Mildly off topic, but is there any chance that you'll get to write a Demon version of Tokyo too? Super excited to see more about Changeling since its one of my favourite lines!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-14T19:54:40-08:00","id":370644,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Second Chances</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/341562-preliminary-outline-for-changeling-the-lost-second-edition?p=370638#post370638\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mildly off topic, but is there any chance that you'll get to write a Demon version of Tokyo too? Super excited to see more about Changeling since its one of my favourite lines!</div> </div> </div> </div>I dunno. Some of us have been trying to find a good space for it, but no luck so far. I know it won't be in the Storyteller Guide.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-18T12:07:25-08:00","id":374363,"title":"","content":"I had a few questions!<br /> <br /> 1. Do you have any plans for Oneriomancy? Will you keep the strange powers the True Fae use in Dream Warping?<br /> <br /> 2. Any mention of the Morpheans and Incubi from Dancers in the Dusk?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2244-nothri","name":"nothri","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"485"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-18T16:06:45-08:00","id":374533,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nothri</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/341562-preliminary-outline-for-changeling-the-lost-second-edition?p=374363#post374363\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I had a few questions!<br /> <br /> 1. Do you have any plans for Oneriomancy? Will you keep the strange powers the True Fae use in Dream Warping?<br /> <br /> 2. Any mention of the Morpheans and Incubi from Dancers in the Dusk?</div> </div> </div> </div>1) Yes. We're going to try to bring Oneiromancy into the fold a little as a more clear and up-front advantage Changeling characters receive. <br /> <br /> 2) Not sure.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-19T00:33:11-08:00","id":374964,"title":"","content":"Nevermind! I see it was removed while you're reviewing. Sorry, I had trouble parsing the post haha. I saw everyone discussing it and assumed it was still live. X)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4769,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4769-mjspra2","user":"mjspra2","date":".  I see my mistake. 01-19-2015, 03:37 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4769-mjspra2","name":"mjspra2","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4769_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"16"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-23T17:36:39-08:00","id":379689,"title":"","content":"What if the Huntsman were really a reflection of the True Fae; except on the other side of the Hedge. In earth, a Changeling wants to build/rebuild a life for itself, and the Huntsman are the manifestations of world, which say 'This is odd. This shouldn't be here. Your story is supposed to be happening in Arcadia, little fae. You're not a person anymore. We much put normalcy back where you've drug your muddy little feet in.&quot;. More a less, it's trying to correct itself because it believes you're not supposed to be there","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/287-wildfire","name":"Wildfire","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"45"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-24T01:59:11-08:00","id":379911,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wildfire</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/341562-preliminary-outline-for-changeling-the-lost-second-edition?p=379689#post379689\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What if the Huntsman were really a reflection of the True Fae; except on the other side of the Hedge. In earth, a Changeling wants to build/rebuild a life for itself, and the Huntsman are the manifestations of world, which say 'This is odd. This shouldn't be here. Your story is supposed to be happening in Arcadia, little fae. You're not a person anymore. We much put normalcy back where you've drug your muddy little feet in.&quot;. More a less, it's trying to correct itself because it believes you're not supposed to be there</div> </div> </div> </div>Eh. We're definitely looking at Huntsmen as &quot;middle men&quot; of sorts. It makes the issue less black/white, and makes them more compelling to deal with.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-26T03:36:36-08:00","id":381724,"title":"","content":"I'm curious how the role of Privateers is changed now that Huntsmen are &quot;middle men&quot; for True Fae. Will there be a sort of rivalry between those groups, as both profit from providing &quot;services&quot; to Gentry?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cI am absolute, I am perfect, I am supreme. I shall be eternal. My tragedy, is that there is no other fate for me. My powerlessness was that I couldn\u2019t subjugate my journey to the gods, while dreaming of rebirth at the end of distant time, like other pharaohs.\u201d Ramesses II, Fate/Prototype: Argent Fragments.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2918-kat","name":"Kat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2918_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1762"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-26T08:30:46-08:00","id":382009,"title":"","content":"I imagine Privateers are one group of the Huntsman.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-26T20:39:45-08:00","id":382663,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kat</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/341562-preliminary-outline-for-changeling-the-lost-second-edition?p=381724#post381724\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm curious how the role of Privateers is changed now that Huntsmen are &quot;middle men&quot; for True Fae. Will there be a sort of rivalry between those groups, as both profit from providing &quot;services&quot; to Gentry?</div> </div> </div> </div>Curious about that too.<br /> <br /> Could possibly work with the huntsmen in a network as scouts. Working with the Huntsmen in return to not becoming there next target or finding out that dealing with them is much more profitable and safer than dealing with the Gentry. Sometimes it's better to deal with the supervisor than the boss man ya know? The privateers do their thing, and aid the hunstmen with any of there marks. Maybe even rewarded to become huntsmen themselves.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><i>&quot;I am a daydreamer and a Night thinker.&quot;~</i></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1820-nightout","name":"Nightout","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1820_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"57"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-27T08:44:16-08:00","id":383158,"title":"","content":"In all honesty, I'm wondering just how mercenary Huntsmen are. Besides Privateers and Loyalists, could a &quot;normal&quot;(if amoral/desperate) Changeling make a deal with these middle-men to make enemies of themselves or the Freehold(which could cover anyone from dissidents to Loyalists) &quot;disappear&quot;?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-27T17:34:52-08:00","id":383841,"title":"","content":"I'd say that thematically there's the possibility for a Huntsman working with (rather than against) the PCs, though it'll always be mistrustful and there'll be tension on both sides. I mean, wasn't the guy who helped cut Red Riding Hood out of her grandma's belly a huntsman?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1168-hobbitguy1420","name":"HobbitGuy1420","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"332"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-27T20:04:24-08:00","id":383919,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HobbitGuy1420</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/341562-preliminary-outline-for-changeling-the-lost-second-edition?p=383841#post383841\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd say that thematically there's the possibility for a Huntsman working with (rather than against) the PCs, though it'll always be mistrustful and there'll be tension on both sides. I mean, wasn't the guy who helped cut Red Riding Hood out of her grandma's belly a huntsman?</div> </div> </div> </div>He was in fact.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-27T21:26:14-08:00","id":383975,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HobbitGuy1420</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/341562-preliminary-outline-for-changeling-the-lost-second-edition?p=383841#post383841\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd say that thematically there's the possibility for a Huntsman working with (rather than against) the PCs, though it'll always be mistrustful and there'll be tension on both sides. I mean, wasn't the guy who helped cut Red Riding Hood out of her grandma's belly a huntsman?</div> </div> </div> </div>Thematically in fairy tales, what a huntsman is probably is someone who is unafraid of the Hedge (i.e., &quot;the woods&quot;) because the Hedge is part and parcel of his life. Changelings are inevitably separate from the Hedge in that they think of it as the wall between them and the Fae, but a huntsman sees the Hedge as the provider of the basic natural resources in his life: food, shelter, etc. <i>Why</i> a huntsman's relationship with the Hedge is the way it is is probably the best indicator for how he'll react to the PCs. I'd expect some low-level huntsmen to be pissed at the PCs simply for taking goblin fruit he considered in his territory, for instance. Changelings who make this shift in their perspective should probably be considered huntsmen, even if they're not actively hunting a Changeling.<br /> <br /> All speculation, naturally, but to me that's the clearest trail of breadcrumbs from the term.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I call the Integrity-analogue the &quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/822559-trying-to-understand-the-morality-system?p=825008#post825008\" target=\"_blank\">subjective stat</a>&quot;.<br /> An explanation how to <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/913221-using-social-manuevering\" target=\"_blank\">use Social Manuevering</a>.<br /> Guanxi Explanations: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=787824#post787824\" target=\"_blank\">1</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=788173#post788173\" target=\"_blank\">2</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/833863-mages-and-trading-favors?p=834531#post834531\" target=\"_blank\">3</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2758-errol216","name":"Errol216","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-27T21:44:16-08:00","id":383990,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HobbitGuy1420</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/341562-preliminary-outline-for-changeling-the-lost-second-edition?p=383841#post383841\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd say that thematically there's the possibility for a Huntsman working with (rather than against) the PCs, though it'll always be mistrustful and there'll be tension on both sides. I mean, wasn't the guy who helped cut Red Riding Hood out of her grandma's belly a huntsman?</div> </div> </div> </div>Also reflected in Snow White.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/614-eolirin","name":"Eolirin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-28T04:34:06-08:00","id":384112,"title":"","content":"I could envision a scenario where Privateers and Huntsmen compete over the same target and even may try to thwart each other's attempts to claim the mark. Which the hunted may exploit in the end.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cI am absolute, I am perfect, I am supreme. I shall be eternal. My tragedy, is that there is no other fate for me. My powerlessness was that I couldn\u2019t subjugate my journey to the gods, while dreaming of rebirth at the end of distant time, like other pharaohs.\u201d Ramesses II, Fate/Prototype: Argent Fragments.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2918-kat","name":"Kat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2918_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1762"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}